172
00:11:14,250 --> 00:11:15,090
[SPEAKER_01] Što sam doživio?

173
00:11:15,390 --> 00:11:21,630
[SPEAKER_00] Well, it turns out that my wife actually wanted me to take a season off of ministry when we got married.

174
00:11:21,930 --> 00:11:30,330
[SPEAKER_01] Uh, ono što se dogodilo je da je moja supruga željela da uzmem vrijeme, da prestanem sa služenjem kad smo se vjenčali.

175
00:11:30,810 --> 00:11:36,630
[SPEAKER_00] It also turns out that she had a prior leg injury, so she didn't want to exercise with me.

176
00:11:37,050 --> 00:11:41,010
[SPEAKER_01] I ispalo je da je prije toga imala jednu ozljedu noge, pa nije mogla vježbati sa mnom.

177
00:11:41,550 --> 00:11:48,810
[SPEAKER_00] And she loves singing and playing music that's already written, and finds writing music very anxiety-inducing.

178
00:11:49,470 --> 00:11:59,010
[SPEAKER_01] I voli pjevati glazbu koja je već—pjesme koje su već napisane, ali je jako prestravljena od toga da sama stvara glazbu i pjeva pjesmu.

179
00:11:59,370 --> 00:12:05,730
[SPEAKER_00] And when it came to physical intimacy, she was—she was very averse to it, um, but I didn't know why at the time.

180
00:12:05,970 --> 00:12:12,750
[SPEAKER_01] Kad je došlo do, uh, do fizičke intimnosti, bila je—to joj je bilo jako odbojno, iako nisam znao zašto u to vrijeme.

181
00:12:13,050 --> 00:12:18,210
[SPEAKER_00] But what I'd been told should have been the easiest part of the honeymoon was actually the biggest struggle for us.

182
00:12:18,390 --> 00:12:22,590
[SPEAKER_01] I ono što je trebalo biti najlakši dio medenog mjeseca, nama je bila najveća poteškoća.

183
00:12:23,250 --> 00:12:28,110
[SPEAKER_00] So just from some of these basic expectations, how many of you can relate to some of that?

184
00:12:28,230 --> 00:12:34,470
[SPEAKER_01] Koliko od vas se može povezati s nekim ovim osnovnim očekivanjima koja se nisu dogodila? Dignite ruku.

185
00:12:37,110 --> 00:12:38,850
[SPEAKER_00] Only a few. Some of you are lying.

186
00:12:39,210 --> 00:12:41,070
[SPEAKER_01] Samo par, a neki od vas lažu.

187
00:12:43,050 --> 00:12:48,030
[SPEAKER_00] So how do we get from common unmet expectations to spiritual complications?

188
00:12:48,210 --> 00:12:53,850
[SPEAKER_01] Kako dođemo od uobičajenih neostvarenih očekivanja do duhovnih komplikacija?

189
00:12:54,030 --> 00:12:57,390
[SPEAKER_00] Well, let me talk about the power of unmet expectations.

190
00:12:57,750 --> 00:13:00,270
[SPEAKER_01] Pričat ću o snazi neispunjenih očekivanja.

191
00:13:00,810 --> 00:13:07,170
[SPEAKER_00] Did any of you in your marriage preparation, those that are married, have to take a compatibility test with your spouse?

192
00:13:07,290 --> 00:13:15,330
[SPEAKER_01] Je li netko od vas pisao ili prolazio sa suprugom tekst test kompatibilnosti? Dignite ruku.

193
00:13:15,390 --> 00:13:15,810
[SPEAKER_00] Anyone?

194
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:16,890
[SPEAKER_01] Bilo tko?

195
00:13:17,190 --> 00:13:20,790
[SPEAKER_00] No. Okay. In the United States, it's very common. It's very common.

196
00:13:20,850 --> 00:13:22,770
[SPEAKER_01] U Sjedinjenim Državama je to jako uobičajeno.

197
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:26,430
[SPEAKER_00] Because the Church wants you to be prepared for what you're up against.

198
00:13:26,610 --> 00:13:29,550
[SPEAKER_01] Jer Crkva želi da budete pripremljeni za ono što vas čeka.

199
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:37,230
[SPEAKER_00] So for us, my wife and I, we were—we were told to take this test, and we got the results, and we sat down with the priest.

200
00:13:37,950 --> 00:13:43,530
[SPEAKER_01] I meni—mojoj ženi i meni su dali da to riješimo, i onda smo sjeli nakon toga skupa sa svećenikom.

201
00:13:44,190 --> 00:13:45,570
[SPEAKER_00] And he looks at them, and he's like...

202
00:13:48,030 --> 00:13:49,050
[SPEAKER_01] Njegova reakcija je bila...

203
00:13:52,110 --> 00:13:55,890
[SPEAKER_00] Says, "Well, you guys scored opposite on almost everything."

204
00:13:56,430 --> 00:14:00,270
[SPEAKER_01] Rekao je: "Vaši rezultati su gotovo suprotni na svemu."

205
00:14:00,630 --> 00:14:02,790
[SPEAKER_00] But if you stick to Jesus, I guess you'll be fine.

206
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:05,430
[SPEAKER_01] Ali ako se budete držali Isusa, bit će vam super.

207
00:14:06,150 --> 00:14:08,070
[SPEAKER_00] Which, there's some truth to that.

208
00:14:08,370 --> 00:14:09,750
[SPEAKER_01] Postoji nešto istine u tome.

209
00:14:10,170 --> 00:14:15,210
[SPEAKER_00] But when we enter marriage with all these unmet expectations, unmet hopes, what do you think happened?

210
00:14:15,450 --> 00:14:19,650
[SPEAKER_01] Ali kad smo ušli u brak sa svim ovim neispunjenim očekivanjima, što mislite, što se dogodilo?

211
00:14:20,010 --> 00:14:22,290
[SPEAKER_00] In the Bible, we call this "deferred hope."

212
00:14:23,130 --> 00:14:27,030
[SPEAKER_01] U Bibliji to zovemo "neispunjena nada."

213
00:14:27,390 --> 00:14:32,430
[SPEAKER_00] Yeah. Proverbs 13:12 says, "Hope deferred makes the heart sick."

214
00:14:33,270 --> 00:14:41,250
[SPEAKER_01] U Proverbs—u Izrekama 13:12 kaže: "Neispunjena nada čini srce bolesnim."

215
00:14:41,910 --> 00:14:42,090
[SPEAKER_00] Yeah.

216
00:14:42,210 --> 00:14:44,370
[SPEAKER_01] To je slobodni prijevod, ovako, nemam tu sad...

217
00:14:47,250 --> 00:14:47,970
[SPEAKER_01] Free translation.

218
00:14:48,450 --> 00:14:51,270
[SPEAKER_00] Free translation. That's awesome.

219
00:14:53,430 --> 00:14:56,310
[SPEAKER_00] But not only what you see on the outside.

220
00:14:56,610 --> 00:14:58,590
[SPEAKER_01] Ne samo ono što vidite na van.

221
00:14:59,070 --> 00:15:03,690
[SPEAKER_00] But often you can see on the inside. There's—there's disappointment, there's rejection, right?

222
00:15:04,170 --> 00:15:07,590
[SPEAKER_01] Iznutra isto se događa razočarenje, odbačenost.

223
00:15:07,770 --> 00:15:11,730
[SPEAKER_00] Because if what I expected doesn't happen, I—I have to do something with that.

224
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:15,750
[SPEAKER_01] Jer ako ono što sam očekivao se nije dogodilo, moram nešto učiniti s time.

225
00:15:15,990 --> 00:15:21,390
[SPEAKER_00] I could feel let down, or—or rejected, or the desires of my heart are off.

226
00:15:21,690 --> 00:15:27,150
[SPEAKER_01] Ili mogu osjećati kao da sam izdan, odbačen, ili da su ugašene moje želje srca.

227
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:30,750
[SPEAKER_00] Or maybe that I'm impressed by this person who won't agree with me.

228
00:15:30,990 --> 00:15:34,530
[SPEAKER_01] Ili da sam impresioniran ovom osobom koja se nikako ne može složiti sa mnom.

229
00:15:35,130 --> 00:15:39,630
[SPEAKER_00] Now, these are natural responses without God, without bringing it to God.

230
00:15:39,870 --> 00:15:45,030
[SPEAKER_01] I to su prirodne reakcije ako ih—ako te osjećaje ne prinesemo Bogu.

231
00:15:45,870 --> 00:15:49,770
[SPEAKER_00] Um, blessed vulnerable Fulton Sheen, very recent.

232
00:15:50,010 --> 00:15:53,550
[SPEAKER_01] Uh, blaženi Fulton Sheen, nedavno proglašen blaženim.

233
00:15:53,610 --> 00:15:57,270
[SPEAKER_00] He once said this: "It takes three to make love, not two."

234
00:15:57,630 --> 00:16:01,350
[SPEAKER_01] Rekao je: "Potrebno je troje da bi se vodila ljubav, ne dvoje."

235
00:16:01,650 --> 00:16:04,470
[SPEAKER_00] It's you, your spouse, and God.

236
00:16:05,070 --> 00:16:07,590
[SPEAKER_01] Ti, tvoja suprug ili supruga, i Bog.

237
00:16:08,130 --> 00:16:12,990
[SPEAKER_00] He says, "Without God, people only succeed in bringing out the worst in each other."

238
00:16:13,590 --> 00:16:17,910
[SPEAKER_01] Bez Boga, ljudi uspijevaju samo izvući najgore jedno iz drugoga.

239
00:16:18,630 --> 00:16:23,790
[SPEAKER_00] But on the other hand, with God, with Jesus, he brings light in your confusion.

240
00:16:24,330 --> 00:16:29,730
[SPEAKER_01] Ali na drugu stranu, s Bogom, s Isusom, on donosi svjetlo

241
00:16:31,170 --> 00:16:34,770
[SPEAKER_01] u vaše konfuzije, u vaše zbunjenosti.

242
00:16:34,950 --> 00:16:36,930
[SPEAKER_00] He reveals, "I'm going to make a way for you."

243
00:16:37,650 --> 00:16:39,330
[SPEAKER_01] Objavljuje nam put za nas.

244
00:16:39,570 --> 00:16:41,670
[SPEAKER_00] Or maybe he has a bigger gift than you expected.

245
00:16:41,910 --> 00:16:44,190
[SPEAKER_01] Ili možda ima veći dar nego što ste očekivali.

246
00:16:44,430 --> 00:16:47,790
[SPEAKER_00] Or maybe he's breaking you free from something that's actually not good for you.

247
00:16:48,090 --> 00:16:50,910
[SPEAKER_01] Ili te možda oslobađa od nečeg što uopće nije dobro za tebe.

248
00:16:51,270 --> 00:16:54,090
[SPEAKER_00] Because when Jesus speaks, he puts hope into your heart.

249
00:16:54,150 --> 00:16:57,210
[SPEAKER_01] Jer kad Isus progovara, on stavlja nadu u srce.

250
00:16:57,690 --> 00:17:01,350
[SPEAKER_00] The Catechism, in paragraph 1608, it says this.

251
00:17:01,650 --> 00:17:04,710
[SPEAKER_01] U Katekizmu 1608 kaže ovo.

252
00:17:05,250 --> 00:17:10,410
[SPEAKER_00] Says, "To heal the wounds of sin, man and woman need the help of the grace."

253
00:17:10,530 --> 00:17:12,810
[SPEAKER_01] Da bi se iscijelile rane grijeha,

254
00:17:14,490 --> 00:17:17,430
[SPEAKER_01] muškarac i žena trebaju pomoć milosti.

255
00:17:17,550 --> 00:17:20,430
[SPEAKER_00] That God, in his infinite mercy, never refuses them.

256
00:17:20,610 --> 00:17:24,510
[SPEAKER_01] Kojom Bog nikad ne uskraćuje u svojoj bezgraničnoj milosti.

257
00:17:24,870 --> 00:17:29,190
[SPEAKER_00] Without his help, man and woman cannot achieve the union of their lives.

258
00:17:29,730 --> 00:17:35,550
[SPEAKER_01] Bez Božje pomoći, muškarac i žena ne mogu postići jedinstvo u svome životu.

259
00:17:35,910 --> 00:17:38,010
[SPEAKER_00] For which God created them in the beginning.

260
00:17:38,430 --> 00:17:40,650
[SPEAKER_01] Za koje ih je Bog stvorio u početku.

261
00:17:41,070 --> 00:17:44,550
[SPEAKER_00] Because without his help, we often fight.

262
00:17:44,670 --> 00:17:46,650
[SPEAKER_01] Bez njegove pomoći se često svađamo.

263
00:17:47,010 --> 00:17:47,670
[SPEAKER_00] Or flight.

264
00:17:48,090 --> 00:17:48,810
[SPEAKER_01] Ili bježimo.

265
00:17:49,470 --> 00:17:53,250
[SPEAKER_00] If God's not our protector, we often fight for control.

266
00:17:53,430 --> 00:17:56,070
[SPEAKER_01] Ako Bog nije naš zaštitnik, borimo se za kontrolu.

267
00:17:56,490 --> 00:17:57,810
[SPEAKER_00] Or we withdraw, we hide.

268
00:17:58,290 --> 00:17:58,890
[SPEAKER_01] Ili se...

269
00:17:59,010 --> 00:17:59,550
[SPEAKER_00] For control.

270
00:17:59,730 --> 00:18:02,970
[SPEAKER_01] Ili se sklanjamo i skrivamo te kontrole.

271
00:18:03,570 --> 00:18:05,610
[SPEAKER_00] But in marriage, when you do this, what happens?

272
00:18:05,970 --> 00:18:08,070
[SPEAKER_01] A u braku, ako to učiniš, što se dogodi?

273
00:18:08,490 --> 00:18:09,570
[SPEAKER_00] It leads to isolation.

274
00:18:10,050 --> 00:18:11,070
[SPEAKER_01] Vodi do izolacije.

275
00:18:11,310 --> 00:18:11,730
[SPEAKER_00] To vision.

276
00:18:12,390 --> 00:18:13,890
[SPEAKER_01] Do odvojenosti.

277
00:18:14,970 --> 00:18:18,090
[SPEAKER_00] Well, who do you think likes isolation and division?

278
00:18:18,330 --> 00:18:21,750
[SPEAKER_01] Što mislite, kome se sviđa izolacija i odvojenost?

279
00:18:22,350 --> 00:18:25,830
[SPEAKER_00] How many of you think it's the one who said it's not good for the man to be alone?

280
00:18:26,490 --> 00:18:34,470
[SPEAKER_01] Što mislite, koliko—koliko od vas misli da je—da se izolacija i odvojenost sviđaju onom koji je rekao: "Za čovjeka nije dobro da bude sam."

281
00:18:36,630 --> 00:18:42,210
[SPEAKER_00] One. Uh-oh. How many of you think it's the one whose name in Greek means "to divide"?

282
00:18:42,930 --> 00:18:50,970
[SPEAKER_01] The devil. A koliko od vas misli da se to sviđa onomu koji—čije ime na grčkom znači "da razdvaja, da odvaja"? Đavao.

283
00:18:51,270 --> 00:18:52,290
[SPEAKER_00] There's more. Okay, okay.

284
00:18:52,530 --> 00:18:52,590
[SPEAKER_01] There

285
00:18:52,650 --> 00:18:52,710
[SPEAKER_00] we

286
00:18:52,770 --> 00:18:53,490
[SPEAKER_01] go. Dobro. Više vas.

287
00:18:53,610 --> 00:18:53,790
[SPEAKER_00] There we

288
00:18:53,850 --> 00:18:54,030
[SPEAKER_02] go.

289
00:18:55,230 --> 00:18:57,630
[SPEAKER_00] Guys, the devil hates marriage.

290
00:18:58,350 --> 00:19:00,270
[SPEAKER_01] Ljudi, đavao mrzi brak.

291
00:19:00,450 --> 00:19:02,190
[SPEAKER_00] He hates it with a burning passion.

292
00:19:02,670 --> 00:19:05,610
[SPEAKER_01] Mrzi ga s gorućom strašću.

293
00:19:06,570 --> 00:19:07,470
[SPEAKER_00] Why does he hate it?

294
00:19:07,710 --> 00:19:08,550
[SPEAKER_01] Zašto ga mrzi?

295
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:10,830
[SPEAKER_00] Because it represents everything he is not.

296
00:19:11,070 --> 00:19:13,230
[SPEAKER_01] Zato što predstavlja sve što on nije.

297
00:19:13,590 --> 00:19:15,870
[SPEAKER_00] It represents everything he cannot have.

298
00:19:16,110 --> 00:19:17,910
[SPEAKER_01] Predstavlja sve što on ne može imati.

299
00:19:18,090 --> 00:19:22,470
[SPEAKER_00] He's literally hellbent on his mission to steal, kill, and destroy us.

300
00:19:22,650 --> 00:19:29,070
[SPEAKER_01] On je—u braku je zaustavljen u misiji da uništava, ubije i ukrade.

301
00:19:29,670 --> 00:19:32,850
[SPEAKER_00] And in my own marriage, he spent years feeding us these lies.

302
00:19:33,330 --> 00:19:36,570
[SPEAKER_01] I u mom braku potrošio je godine hraneći nas tim lažima.

303
00:19:37,230 --> 00:19:39,270
[SPEAKER_00] Say things like, "You guys are so different."

304
00:19:39,690 --> 00:19:41,730
[SPEAKER_01] Govoreći kao: "Vi ste toliko drugačiji."

305
00:19:42,030 --> 00:19:43,650
[SPEAKER_00] I don't know if you're ever going to be happy.

306
00:19:44,130 --> 00:19:46,050
[SPEAKER_01] Ne znam hoćete li ikad biti sretni skupa.

307
00:19:46,290 --> 00:19:48,150
[SPEAKER_00] Has anything turned out how you expected?

308
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:50,070
[SPEAKER_01] Je li išta bilo kako si očekivao?

309
00:19:50,430 --> 00:19:51,810
[SPEAKER_00] Maybe you made the wrong decision.

310
00:19:51,990 --> 00:19:53,370
[SPEAKER_01] Možda si donio krivu odluku.

311
00:19:53,910 --> 00:19:55,290
[SPEAKER_00] Does this sound familiar to anyone?

312
00:19:55,410 --> 00:19:56,730
[SPEAKER_01] Da li vam to zvuči poznato?

313
00:19:58,650 --> 00:20:03,930
[SPEAKER_00] Guys, the devil will do everything he can to cast suspicion or insecurity on our marriages.

314
00:20:04,530 --> 00:20:10,890
[SPEAKER_01] Đavo će učiniti sve što može da posije strah i sumnju, i odvoj—i razdvojenost u naše brakove.

315
00:20:11,130 --> 00:20:15,810
[SPEAKER_00] Because if he can divide us, we find ourselves apart from the very reason why we're made.

316
00:20:16,470 --> 00:20:21,330
[SPEAKER_01] I ako nas uspije odvojiti, odvojeni smo od samog smisla za ono što smo stvoreni.

317
00:20:21,750 --> 00:20:24,390
[SPEAKER_00] Because we were made for love, for relationship.

318
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:26,610
[SPEAKER_01] Jer smo stvoreni za odnos i za ljubav.

319
00:20:27,270 --> 00:20:30,390
[SPEAKER_00] For vulnerable, exposed relationship.

320
00:20:30,810 --> 00:20:33,930
[SPEAKER_01] Za ranjiv, otvoren odnos.

321
00:20:34,470 --> 00:20:38,670
[SPEAKER_00] I remember when we got married, um, some of our friends wrote us a wedding card.

322
00:20:39,090 --> 00:20:45,390
[SPEAKER_01] Sjećam se kad smo se vjenčali, neki od nas prije—naših prijatelji su nam napisali čestitku za vjenčanje.

323
00:20:46,170 --> 00:20:52,290
[SPEAKER_00] Inside it said, "If you ever get in an argument, the best thing you can do is just get naked."

324
00:20:53,250 --> 00:20:58,470
[SPEAKER_01] I unutra je pisalo: "Ako uđete u svađu, najbolje što možete napraviti je samo se skinuti goli."

325
00:20:58,890 --> 00:21:00,870
[SPEAKER_00] Now, I think they were trying to be funny.

326
00:21:01,170 --> 00:21:03,570
[SPEAKER_01] Mislim da su pokušali biti šaljivi.

327
00:21:04,050 --> 00:21:09,750
[SPEAKER_00] But I want you to think about this. You have the first man, first woman, in the garden, completely exposed.

328
00:21:10,470 --> 00:21:16,710
[SPEAKER_01] I želim da razmislite o ovome: imate prvog čovjeka i prvu ženu u raju, potpuno goli, potpuno ogoljeni.

329
00:21:17,250 --> 00:21:18,390
[SPEAKER_00] Total self-gift.

330
00:21:18,870 --> 00:21:20,250
[SPEAKER_01] Potpuno sebedarije.

331
00:21:20,970 --> 00:21:22,110
[SPEAKER_00] Now I want you to look at Jesus.

332
00:21:22,890 --> 00:21:24,330
[SPEAKER_01] Želim da pogledate na Isusa.

333
00:21:24,630 --> 00:21:25,710
[SPEAKER_00] There we go. On the cross.

334
00:21:25,890 --> 00:21:26,550
[SPEAKER_01] Tamo na križu.

335
00:21:27,330 --> 00:21:29,910
[SPEAKER_00] Vulnerable, exposed. Ranjen.

336
00:21:30,030 --> 00:21:30,450
[SPEAKER_01] Ogoljen.

337
00:21:31,110 --> 00:21:32,010
[SPEAKER_00] Total self-gift.

338
00:21:32,310 --> 00:21:33,330
[SPEAKER_01] Potpuno sebedarije.

339
00:21:35,190 --> 00:21:38,610
[SPEAKER_00] In both our joys and our trials, this is why we're made.

340
00:21:38,850 --> 00:21:41,730
[SPEAKER_01] I u našim radostima i poteškoćama, za to smo stvoreni.

341
00:21:42,150 --> 00:21:44,070
[SPEAKER_00] To behold and love others.

342
00:21:44,790 --> 00:21:46,770
[SPEAKER_01] Da druge volimo i čuvamo.

343
00:21:47,010 --> 00:21:49,170
[SPEAKER_00] And to let ourselves be beheld and loved.

344
00:21:49,410 --> 00:21:52,290
[SPEAKER_01] I da dopustimo da i mi sami budemo ljubljeni i čuvani.

345
00:21:53,970 --> 00:21:56,130
[SPEAKER_00] Catechism 1604 says this.

346
00:21:56,370 --> 00:21:58,950
[SPEAKER_01] Katekizam 1604 kaže ovo.

347
