[SPEAKER_01] Na različitim dijelovima kauča nije kvalitetno vrijeme provedeno zajedno.

524
00:32:35,490 --> 00:32:40,650
[SPEAKER_00] And I'd also say this: working together on something isn't the fulfillment of quality time either.

525
00:32:40,890 --> 00:32:45,270
[SPEAKER_01] I čak i to da radimo nešto zajedno nije provođenje kvalitetnog vremena zajedno.

526
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:51,210
[SPEAKER_00] I've heard this—this quote from a French author used many times to describe marriage.

527
00:32:51,690 --> 00:32:56,070
[SPEAKER_01] Čuo sam ovu izjavu jednog francuskog autora koja opisuje brak.

528
00:32:56,970 --> 00:33:00,690
[SPEAKER_00] That love doesn't consist of gazing at each other.

529
00:33:01,290 --> 00:33:05,130
[SPEAKER_01] Ljubav nije—ljubav se ne sastoji u tome da gledamo jedno u drugo.

530
00:33:05,490 --> 00:33:07,950
[SPEAKER_00] But in looking outward together in the same direction.

531
00:33:08,070 --> 00:33:11,430
[SPEAKER_01] Nego da zajedno gledamo vani u istom smjeru.

532
00:33:11,670 --> 00:33:13,530
[SPEAKER_00] Has anyone heard this in the context of marriage?

533
00:33:13,590 --> 00:33:15,330
[SPEAKER_01] Je li netko to čuo u kontekstu braka?

534
00:33:15,510 --> 00:33:16,590
[SPEAKER_00] Yeah. It sounds great.

535
00:33:17,550 --> 00:33:18,270
[SPEAKER_01] Zvuči odlično.

536
00:33:18,930 --> 00:33:22,650
[SPEAKER_00] There's this—this semblance of unity and teamwork.

537
00:33:22,830 --> 00:33:26,970
[SPEAKER_01] Ovaj—taj osjećaj zajedništva i jedinstva i timskog rada.

538
00:33:27,270 --> 00:33:32,970
[SPEAKER_00] And I love that. I—as you remember, I wanted my wife to join me in everything, working together.

539
00:33:33,210 --> 00:33:37,530
[SPEAKER_01] Sviđa mi se to. I htio sam da mi se moja supruga pridruži u tome da sve zajedno radimo.

540
00:33:37,890 --> 00:33:39,210
[SPEAKER_00] But there's a problem with this.

541
00:33:39,390 --> 00:33:40,650
[SPEAKER_01] Ali postoji problem s time.

542
00:33:40,890 --> 00:33:45,510
[SPEAKER_00] Because if this is the focus, your love is always being directed outward.

543
00:33:45,990 --> 00:33:49,650
[SPEAKER_01] Jer ako je to tvoj fokus, tvoja ljubav je uvijek usmjerena na van.

544
00:33:50,070 --> 00:33:53,910
[SPEAKER_00] And true or false, your spouse needs to receive your love.

545
00:33:54,510 --> 00:34:00,750
[SPEAKER_01] I bilo to istinito ili ne, tvoj supružnik, tvoja supruga trebaju primiti tvoju ljubav.

546
00:34:02,250 --> 00:34:02,550
[SPEAKER_00] Da.

547
00:34:03,570 --> 00:34:03,750
[SPEAKER_01] Da.

548
00:34:05,070 --> 00:34:08,190
[SPEAKER_00] Now, charity—this looking outward—it's very important.

549
00:34:08,670 --> 00:34:11,490
[SPEAKER_01] I ta ljubav koja se daje na van je jako potrebna.

550
00:34:11,910 --> 00:34:16,050
[SPEAKER_00] But true quality time in marriage, you have to behold the other.

551
00:34:16,650 --> 00:34:21,930
[SPEAKER_01] I da bi proveli zajedno vrijeme kvalitetno skupa, morate paziti jedno na drugo.

552
00:34:22,110 --> 00:34:23,250
[SPEAKER_00] You have to see the other.

553
00:34:23,490 --> 00:34:24,810
[SPEAKER_01] Morate vidjeti drugog.

554
00:34:25,350 --> 00:34:33,030
[SPEAKER_00] And I'd argue that quality time, in terms of quality, is going to be measured by how much your spouse experiences being seen.

555
00:34:33,870 --> 00:34:44,070
[SPEAKER_01] I vjerujem da će se kvaliteta—i ta kvaliteta u toj riječi—ugledavati u tome koliko se supruga ili suprug osjećalo viđenim i shvaćenim.

556
00:34:44,430 --> 00:34:49,050
[SPEAKER_00] By them first and regularly being the direct recipient of your love.

557
00:34:49,290 --> 00:34:53,070
[SPEAKER_01] Da oni prvi direktno budu primatelji tvoje ljubavi.

558
00:34:53,730 --> 00:34:58,050
[SPEAKER_00] In Encounter, we have this saying that all fruitful ministry flows out of identity.

559
00:34:58,830 --> 00:35:03,090
[SPEAKER_01] U Encounteru kažemo da svako plodno djelovanje i služenje

560
00:35:04,350 --> 00:35:05,970
[SPEAKER_01] proizlazi iz identiteta.

561
00:35:06,390 --> 00:35:11,190
[SPEAKER_00] And that means before we teach anyone to prophesy or heal the sick...

562
00:35:11,430 --> 00:35:15,990
[SPEAKER_01] I prije nego što bilo koga učimo da prorokuje ili ozdravlja bolesne.

563
00:35:16,470 --> 00:35:23,370
[SPEAKER_00] They spend an entire quarter talking with God, experiencing being seen, being known first.

564
00:35:23,730 --> 00:35:30,810
[SPEAKER_01] Provode cijeli semestar prvo upoznavajući Boga i da Bog—da spoznaju da i Bog vidi i poznaje njih.

565
00:35:31,050 --> 00:35:38,010
[SPEAKER_00] And then out of that place, we equip them to heal the sick, to raise the dead, and all the other amazing things.

566
00:35:38,190 --> 00:35:44,190
[SPEAKER_01] I onda ih iz tog mjesta opremamo da liječe bolesne, uskrisuju mrtve i sve ostale prekrasne stvari.

567
00:35:44,670 --> 00:35:46,830
[SPEAKER_00] Our marriages are called to do the same.

568
00:35:47,190 --> 00:35:50,130
[SPEAKER_01] I isto se—isto vrijedi i za naše brakove.

569
00:35:50,550 --> 00:35:52,530
[SPEAKER_00] We love because he first loved us.

570
00:35:52,830 --> 00:35:54,750
[SPEAKER_01] Mi ljubimo zato što je on nas prvi ljubio.

571
00:35:57,870 --> 00:36:00,270
[SPEAKER_00] In the Old Testament, in Deuteronomy, it says this.

572
00:36:01,350 --> 00:36:04,950
[SPEAKER_01] U Knjizi Ponovljenog zakona u Starom zavjetu kaže ovako.

573
00:36:05,850 --> 00:36:08,310
[SPEAKER_00] If you want to look it up: Deuteronomy 24:5.

574
00:36:13,290 --> 00:36:29,610
[SPEAKER_00] While you're looking it up, I'll read it out. It says—24:5—says, "When a man is newly wed, he shall not go out on a military expedition, nor shall any duty be imposed on him.

575
00:36:29,670 --> 00:36:36,330
[SPEAKER_00] He shall be exempt for one year for the sake of his family, to bring joy to the wife he has married."

576
00:36:44,970 --> 00:36:46,290
[SPEAKER_01] That's not it. Sorry.

577
00:36:46,470 --> 00:36:48,510
[SPEAKER_00] Chapter 24, verse 5. Deuteronomy.

578
00:36:54,330 --> 00:36:55,050
[SPEAKER_01] 24:5.

579
00:36:55,230 --> 00:36:55,410
[SPEAKER_00] Yes.

580
00:36:55,650 --> 00:37:04,410
[SPEAKER_01] Kad se tko ne to može ni neka ne ide u vojsku, neka mu se ne dodjeljuje nikakva služba, nego oslobođen neka ostane kod kuće godinu dana da razveseljuje ženu koju je doveo.

581
00:37:05,430 --> 00:37:05,610
[SPEAKER_00] Yeah.

582
00:37:05,730 --> 00:37:05,910
[SPEAKER_01] Yes.

583
00:37:06,270 --> 00:37:07,110
[SPEAKER_00] Have you guys heard this?

584
00:37:07,290 --> 00:37:08,370
[SPEAKER_01] Jeste li to ikada čuli?

585
00:37:08,430 --> 00:37:11,430
[SPEAKER_00] You heard this. Okay. I missed this in my Bible reading.

586
00:37:11,910 --> 00:37:14,070
[SPEAKER_01] Ja sam ovo propustio u svom čitanju Biblije.

587
00:37:14,490 --> 00:37:23,310
[SPEAKER_00] Can you imagine what our marriages would look like if we took an entire year from the beginning of marriage just to pour joy into our spouse?

588
00:37:23,790 --> 00:37:30,630
[SPEAKER_01] Zamislite kako bi izgledali naši brakovi da uzmemo punu godinu dana da samo razveseljujemo svoju suprugu ili supruga.

589
00:37:30,930 --> 00:37:31,770
[SPEAKER_00] And did I do that?

590
00:37:31,950 --> 00:37:33,030
[SPEAKER_01] Jesam li ja to učinio?

591
00:37:33,210 --> 00:37:33,810
[SPEAKER_00] Of course not.

592
00:37:34,050 --> 00:37:34,830
[SPEAKER_01] Naravno da nisam.

593
00:37:35,730 --> 00:37:38,130
[SPEAKER_00] No. To prove I was a worthy husband.

594
00:37:38,250 --> 00:37:40,350
[SPEAKER_01] Da bih dokazao da sam vrijedan muž.

595
00:37:40,470 --> 00:37:42,390
[SPEAKER_00] I got preoccupied with staying busy.

596
00:37:43,170 --> 00:37:45,690
[SPEAKER_01] Preokupirao sam se time da sam bio zaposlen.

597
00:37:45,870 --> 00:37:48,390
[SPEAKER_00] I took a promotion. I took longer hours at work.

598
00:37:48,570 --> 00:37:53,310
[SPEAKER_01] Radio sam prekovremene na poslu, prihvatio sam promaknuće.

599
00:37:53,610 --> 00:37:56,010
[SPEAKER_00] We bought a house. I was buying things for the house.

600
00:37:56,250 --> 00:37:58,530
[SPEAKER_01] Kupio sam kuću, kupovali smo stvari za kuću.

601
00:37:58,950 --> 00:38:01,170
[SPEAKER_00] Getting a puppy and regretting getting a puppy.

602
00:38:01,470 --> 00:38:04,350
[SPEAKER_01] Uzeli smo psa, pa onda smo zažalili što smo uzeli psa.

603
00:38:05,610 --> 00:38:09,390
[SPEAKER_00] And somehow I found a way to get right back into leading ministry.

604
00:38:09,630 --> 00:38:12,510
[SPEAKER_01] I nekako sam se vratio nazad tome da vodim službu.

605
00:38:12,750 --> 00:38:14,730
[SPEAKER_00] And this became a huge source of tension.

606
00:38:14,970 --> 00:38:17,250
[SPEAKER_01] I to je postao veliki izvor napetosti.

607
00:38:17,370 --> 00:38:19,530
[SPEAKER_00] Because as I invested in ministry...

608
00:38:19,890 --> 00:38:21,630
[SPEAKER_01] Jer kako sam ulagao u služenje...

609
00:38:21,990 --> 00:38:23,190
[SPEAKER_00] It was bearing a lot of fruit.

610
00:38:23,670 --> 00:38:25,050
[SPEAKER_01] Donosilo je jako puno ploda.

611
00:38:25,290 --> 00:38:27,330
[SPEAKER_00] So what did I do? I poured more into it.

612
00:38:27,510 --> 00:38:29,790
[SPEAKER_01] I što sam napravio? Još sam više počeo služiti.

613
00:38:30,030 --> 00:38:33,990
[SPEAKER_00] And then I'm telling my wife, "Why are you so sad? You should be doing this."

614
00:38:34,110 --> 00:38:37,470
[SPEAKER_01] I onda govorim svojoj ženi: "Zašto si tako tužna? I ti bi trebala služiti."

615
00:38:37,770 --> 00:38:40,770
[SPEAKER_00] And what I wasn't realizing was that she needed ministry herself.

616
00:38:41,010 --> 00:38:43,890
[SPEAKER_01] A ono što nisam shvatio je da je i njoj bilo potrebno služenje.

617
00:38:44,130 --> 00:38:47,370
[SPEAKER_00] She needed love and attention from those that were closest to her.

618
00:38:47,970 --> 00:38:51,390
[SPEAKER_01] Bila joj je potrebna ljubav i pažnja od onih koji su joj bili najbliži.

619
00:38:51,750 --> 00:38:55,590
[SPEAKER_00] And she needed patient love, the kind that could just be with her when she felt lost.

620
00:38:55,710 --> 00:39:01,950
[SPEAKER_01] Trebala joj je strpljiva ljubav koja je mogla biti s njom u onim trenucima kada se osjećala izgubljeno.

621
00:39:02,610 --> 00:39:05,010
[SPEAKER_00] Now, honestly, that's not my go-to.

622
00:39:05,550 --> 00:39:08,910
[SPEAKER_01] Iskreno, to nije način na koji ja volim davati ljubav.

623
00:39:09,450 --> 00:39:13,590
[SPEAKER_00] I like to problem-solve. I like to take risks, go and try things out.

624
00:39:13,710 --> 00:39:16,710
[SPEAKER_01] Ja volim riskirati, isprobavati stvari, rješavati probleme.

625
00:39:17,250 --> 00:39:21,030
[SPEAKER_00] In the United States, we have this thing called a Strength Finders assessment.

626
00:39:21,270 --> 00:39:25,470
[SPEAKER_01] U SAD-u imamo testove gdje pronalazite svoje jake strane.

627
00:39:25,950 --> 00:39:30,870
[SPEAKER_00] My top strength is Activator, with this tagline: "Is often impatient."

628
00:39:31,590 --> 00:39:36,630
[SPEAKER_01] Moja—moj naziv bi bio Aktivator, onaj koji je često nestrpljiv.

629
00:39:37,530 --> 00:39:40,650
[SPEAKER_00] We also have another that's called the Working Genius assessment.

630
00:39:40,890 --> 00:39:44,970
[SPEAKER_01] Onda imamo drugu koja se kaže Working Genius, ono, radni genij.

631
00:39:45,210 --> 00:39:47,370
[SPEAKER_00] I have Tenacity and Galvanizing.

632
00:39:48,030 --> 00:39:55,530
[SPEAKER_01] Imam... Rješavanje problema i motiviranje.

633
00:39:56,910 --> 00:40:09,270
[SPEAKER_00] Can we give him a hand? He's doing great. I'll translate. It means, "I'm eager to get things moving and to get you moving with me."

634
00:40:09,690 --> 00:40:15,210
[SPEAKER_01] Prevest ću: "Jako sam založen da se pokrenu stvari i da se vi pokrenete sa mnom."

635
00:40:15,390 --> 00:40:19,890
[SPEAKER_00] And if someone's not ready to move, I would just move to those that are.

636
00:40:20,250 --> 00:40:24,030
[SPEAKER_01] I ako netko nije spreman pokrenuti se, otišao bi onima koji jesu spremni.

637
00:40:24,510 --> 00:40:31,410
[SPEAKER_00] Now, in ministry, that can be really great. Those are—those are signs of, like, an evangelist or what we call a harvester.

638
00:40:32,070 --> 00:40:38,910
[SPEAKER_01] To u evangelizaciji može biti dobro. To su znakovi evangelizatora ili onoga koji ide i kupi—koji sije puno plodova.

639
00:40:39,150 --> 00:40:40,650
[SPEAKER_00] And the church does need more of these.

640
00:40:40,890 --> 00:40:42,510
[SPEAKER_01] I crkvi je potrebno takvih ljudi.

641
00:40:43,230 --> 00:40:47,250
[SPEAKER_00] But in marriage, you can't just move on to someone else who's ready.

642
00:40:47,730 --> 00:40:51,090
[SPEAKER_01] Ali u braku ne možeš otići do nekog drugog koji je spreman.

643
00:40:51,750 --> 00:40:54,810
[SPEAKER_00] So I started spending more time in outside ministry.

644
00:40:55,050 --> 00:40:58,350
[SPEAKER_01] Počeo sam provoditi više vremena vani u služenju.

645
00:40:59,850 --> 00:41:03,150
[SPEAKER_00] And as I was succeeding as a professional minister...

646
00:41:03,390 --> 00:41:07,530
[SPEAKER_01] I kako sam uspijevao u tome da sam—da profesionalno služim drugima.

647
00:41:07,890 --> 00:41:13,530
[SPEAKER_00] I was cultivating an environment for deeper wounds of rejection and abandonment with my wife.

648
00:41:13,830 --> 00:41:22,410
[SPEAKER_01] Kultivirao sam atmosferu u kojoj se moja žena još dublje ulazila u ranu odbačenosti i...

649
00:41:23,730 --> 00:41:24,510
[SPEAKER_01] Of rejection and...

650
00:41:24,630 --> 00:41:25,230
[SPEAKER_00] Abandonment.

651
00:41:25,290 --> 00:41:27,030
[SPEAKER_01] I ostavljenosti, napuštenosti. Yeah.

652
00:41:27,570 --> 00:41:33,570
[SPEAKER_00] And the environment I cultivated was influenced by everything that I did outside of the home.

653
00:41:33,690 --> 00:41:38,670
[SPEAKER_01] I to okruženje se povećavalo sa svime onime što sam radio izvan kuće.

654
00:41:39,030 --> 00:41:41,970
[SPEAKER_00] Communicating this: we move at a fast pace.

655
00:41:42,810 --> 00:41:45,930
[SPEAKER_01] Kad sam komunicirao, mi idemo brzim tempom.

656
00:41:47,490 --> 00:41:54,570
[SPEAKER_00] And time with my wife was often spent diagnosing: "How can we fix you and catch you up to speed?"

657
00:41:55,230 --> 00:42:03,690
[SPEAKER_01] I često sam komunicirao sa ženom na način da sam joj govorio kako možemo riješiti tvoje probleme i dovesti te u ovaj brzi tempo.

658
00:42:04,230 --> 00:42:07,290
[SPEAKER_00] How many of you went to Medjugorje with the JP TOOR Healing Center recently?

659
00:42:07,470 --> 00:42:09,510
[SPEAKER_01] Koliko od vas je bilo u Međugorju na

660
00:42:10,830 --> 00:42:14,610
[SPEAKER_01] susretu sa John Paul II za unutarnje ozdravljenje?

661
00:42:15,330 --> 00:42:16,050
[SPEAKER_00] A few of you. Okay.

662
00:42:16,110 --> 00:42:16,770
[SPEAKER_01] Od Bob Schutza?

663
00:42:17,250 --> 00:42:18,390
[SPEAKER_00] Bob Schutz. There you go.

664
00:42:20,310 --> 00:42:21,030
[SPEAKER_01] Prilično slično.

665
00:42:21,330 --> 00:42:25,710
[SPEAKER_00] Yes. Sister Miriam often says this powerful line.

666
00:42:25,950 --> 00:42:28,950
[SPEAKER_01] Sestra Miriam kaže često ovu snažnu rečenicu.

667
00:42:29,250 --> 00:42:32,970
[SPEAKER_00] She says, "You are not a problem to be fixed; you are a person to be loved."

668
00:42:33,450 --> 00:42:38,190
[SPEAKER_01] Ti nisi problem koji treba popraviti, nego osoba koju treba ljubiti.

669
00:42:38,610 --> 00:42:41,250
[SPEAKER_00] The first time I heard this, it cut me to the heart.

670
00:42:41,490 --> 00:42:44,070
[SPEAKER_01] Prvi put kad sam to čuo, pogodilo me ravno u srce.

671
00:42:44,250 --> 00:42:46,530
[SPEAKER_00] Because that's exactly how I'd been treating my wife.

672
00:42:46,770 --> 00:42:50,490
[SPEAKER_01] Jer to je baš bio način na koji sam se ja postavljao prema svojoj ženi.

673
00:42:51,030 --> 00:42:52,050
[SPEAKER_00] You ready for another one?

674
00:42:52,350 --> 00:42:53,490
[SPEAKER_01] Jeste spremni za još jednu?

675
00:42:53,970 --> 00:42:58,590
[SPEAKER_00] Saint Vincent de Paul says, "The one who hurries delays the things of God."

676
00:42:58,830 --> 00:43:04,050
[SPEAKER_01] Sveti Vincent Paulski kaže: "Onaj tko žuri, odgađa Božje stvari."

677
00:43:05,130 --> 00:43:10,230
[SPEAKER_00] So six years into our marriage, when we hit a crisis and had no idea how to fix our marriage...

678
00:43:10,590 --> 00:43:18,630
[SPEAKER_01] Nakon 6 godina braka, kad smo došli do velike krize, nismo znali kako popraviti naš brak.

679
00:43:19,410 --> 00:43:22,650
[SPEAKER_00] I felt Holy Spirit telling me, "Kevin, just show up."

680
00:43:22,950 --> 00:43:26,850
[SPEAKER_01] Osjetio sam da me Duh Sveti poziva da se samo pojavim, da budem prisutan.

681
00:43:27,270 --> 00:43:30,930
[SPEAKER_00] Don't have an agenda, no distractions, just be.

682
00:43:31,470 --> 00:43:34,950
[SPEAKER_01] Nemoj imati planove, nemoj imati akcije, samo budi.

683
00:43:35,910 --> 00:43:38,490
[SPEAKER_00] I'm like, okay, how do I do that?

684
00:43:39,030 --> 00:43:41,010
[SPEAKER_01] U redu. Kako da to napravim?

685
00:43:42,270 --> 00:43:45,630
[SPEAKER_00] Well, I got in this habit of every night, after the kids are in bed...

686
00:43:46,590 --> 00:43:50,730
[SPEAKER_01] Uzeo sam ovu naviku da kad su—kad djeca legnu spavati u krevet...

687
00:43:51,330 --> 00:43:56,430
[SPEAKER_00] I would just go to the couch without my phone, without the TV on, no distractions.

688
00:43:56,850 --> 00:44:00,930
[SPEAKER_01] Sjeo bih na kauč, bez telefona, bez upaljenog TV-a, bez distrakcija.

689
00:44:01,170 --> 00:44:03,390
[SPEAKER_00] And I would just wait, still.

690
00:44:03,510 --> 00:44:04,830
[SPEAKER_01] I samo bih mirno čekao.

691
00:44:05,550 --> 00:44:06,690
[SPEAKER_00] Like a crazy person.

692
00:44:07,050 --> 00:44:07,770
[SPEAKER_01] Kao neki luđak.

693
00:44:09,330 --> 00:44:13,770
[SPEAKER_00] And if my wife wanted to come join me, she could. If not, I would just stay there and pray.

694
00:44:14,310 --> 00:44:20,070
[SPEAKER_01] I ako se moja žena htjela doći pridružiti mi se, super. Ako ne, ostao bih tamo i molio.

695
00:44:21,030 --> 00:44:25,770
[SPEAKER_00] And I would talk to the Lord, but I was posturing myself to be interrupted at any moment.

696
00:44:27,270 --> 00:44:32,130
[SPEAKER_01] Razgovarao sam s Bogom, ali sam se postavljao tako da mi se u bilo kojem trenutku može prekinuti.

697
00:44:32,670 --> 00:44:34,590
[SPEAKER_00] Because you can't force quality time.

698
00:44:34,710 --> 00:44:38,130
[SPEAKER_01] Jer ne možeš natjerati i isforsirati kvalitetno vrijeme.

699
00:44:38,430 --> 00:44:40,770
[SPEAKER_00] But you can posture yourself for receptivity.

700
00:44:41,070 --> 00:44:43,470
[SPEAKER_01] Ali možeš se postaviti tako da ga možeš primiti.

701
00:44:44,130 --> 00:44:48,450
[SPEAKER_00] And if you do this, you're essentially meeting your spouse at their level, at their pace.

702
00:44:48,930 --> 00:44:57,870
[SPEAKER_01] I ako se tako postaviš, postavljaš se da možeš svog supružnika ili suprugu dočekati na njihovoj razini i u njihovom tempu.

703
00:44:58,290 --> 00:45:03,030
[SPEAKER_00] It's like a three-legged race. You have to sync your pace with the other.

704
00:45:03,090 --> 00:45:09,630
[SPEAKER_01] To je kao kad se utrkujete s tri noge, ono, jedna noga vam je zavezana, zajednička. Morate se uskladiti u brzini.

705
00:45:10,710 --> 00:45:16,050
[SPEAKER_00] Something that's really interesting: there's psychological studies of something called heart sync.

706
00:45:17,430 --> 00:45:23,790
[SPEAKER_01] Postoje istraživanja, psihološka, koja govore o sinkronizaciji srca.

707
00:45:24,870 --> 00:45:31,170
[SPEAKER_00] Out of Princeton University, there was this study that said, "When people are emotionally attuned..."

708
00:45:32,010 --> 00:45:34,290
[SPEAKER_01] U trenutku... na Princetonu su istraživali kad su

709
00:45:35,610 --> 00:45:42,750
[SPEAKER_01] ljudi emocionalno nisu spojivi, nisu spojeni, nisu se našli.

710
00:45:42,990 --> 00:45:45,690
[SPEAKER_00] And they're engaged in back-and-forth discussion.

711
00:45:46,230 --> 00:45:49,530
[SPEAKER_01] I cijelo vrijeme su uključeni u nekakve rasprave i diskusije.

712
00:45:50,250 --> 00:45:53,310
[SPEAKER_00] Their heart rates physically synchronize.

713
00:45:53,490 --> 00:45:56,610
[SPEAKER_01] Njihova se srca fizički sinkroniziraju.

714
00:45:57,150 --> 00:46:04,590
[SPEAKER_00] And when their hearts physically synchronize, the study showed they were 70% more likely to share joint decision-making.

715
00:46:04,830 --> 00:46:11,670
[SPEAKER_01] I u trenutku kad se njihova srca sinkroniziraju, 70% je veća šansa da dođu do zajedničke odluke.

716
00:46:12,990 --> 00:46:14,010
[SPEAKER_00] Isn't that awesome?

717
00:46:14,370 --> 00:46:15,330
[SPEAKER_01] Zar to nije zanimljivo?

718
00:46:15,750 --> 00:46:21,210
[SPEAKER_00] Like, scientifically, it shows us: if you want agreement in your marriage, you have to sync your pace.

719
00:46:21,810 --> 00:46:28,170
[SPEAKER_01] Ako želite doći do zajedničkog rješenja u braku, morate doći do zajedničke brzine, zajedničkog tempa.

720
00:46:28,350 --> 00:46:29,490
[SPEAKER_00] And meet them at their level.

721
00:46:30,150 --> 00:46:34,590
[SPEAKER_01] I doći do zajedničkog tempa svog supružnika.

722
00:46:34,890 --> 00:46:42,090
[SPEAKER_00] Now, for those of you in ministry, if their level is slower than the pace of your ministry...

723
00:46:42,270 --> 00:46:48,030
[SPEAKER_01] Za vas koji služite, ako je tempo vašeg supružnika sporiji od vaše službe...

724
00:46:48,390 --> 00:46:51,450
[SPEAKER_00] That means you either have to slow down or step away.

725
00:46:51,810 --> 00:46:56,190
[SPEAKER_01] To znači: ili morate usporiti, ili morate odstupiti sa svog mjesta.

726
00:46:56,790 --> 00:47:02,790
[SPEAKER_00] One of the things my wife told me when she was feeling really hurt was, "Kevin, you love the ministry more than me."

727
00:47:03,030 --> 00:47:09,690
[SPEAKER_01] U jednom trenutku moja žena mi je rekla: "Kevine, voliš više svoju službu nego što voliš mene."

728
00:47:10,050 --> 00:47:12,390
[SPEAKER_00] Now, I personally knew that wasn't true.

729
00:47:12,750 --> 00:47:14,490
[SPEAKER_01] Ja sam znao da to nije istina. But

730
00:47:14,610 --> 00:47:18,870
[SPEAKER_00] if she's believing that and telling me that, it shows me we are way out of sync.

731
00:47:19,650 --> 00:47:25,770
[SPEAKER_01] I ako ona u to vjeruje i to mi govori, znači da smo mi jako daleko od toga da budemo sinkronizirani.

732
00:47:26,070 --> 00:47:32,790
[SPEAKER_00] I remember I brought that to my spiritual director, and his response was, "Kevin, I think you need to let go of the ministry."

733
00:47:33,210 --> 00:47:39,210
[SPEAKER_01] Kad sam to rekao svom duhovniku, on mi je rekao: "Kevine, mislim da moraš napustiti službu."

734
00:47:39,450 --> 00:47:40,290
[SPEAKER_00] And I said, "Yeah?"

735
00:47:40,830 --> 00:47:41,970
[SPEAKER_01] Pitao sam se: "Stvarno?"

736
00:47:43,410 --> 00:47:46,770
[SPEAKER_00] And over the years, I'd been building a ministry team.

737
00:47:46,950 --> 00:47:50,070
[SPEAKER_01] A kroz godine sam izgrađivao tim s kojim smo služili.

738
00:47:50,370 --> 00:47:54,630
[SPEAKER_00] I had hundreds of people coming every week, with 35 to 40 volunteers helping me.

739
00:47:54,870 --> 00:48:01,590
[SPEAKER_01] Imali smo stotine ljudi koji su dolazili svakog tjedna, i 35 do 40 ljudi koji su zajedno sa mnom služili.

740
00:48:01,890 --> 00:48:04,050
[SPEAKER_00] And no one willing to step up and lead.

741
00:48:04,650 --> 00:48:06,690
[SPEAKER_01] Nitko nije želio preuzeti vodeću ulogu.

742
00:48:07,530 --> 00:48:09,690
[SPEAKER_00] But I sent a resignation email the next day.

743
00:48:09,930 --> 00:48:13,650
[SPEAKER_01] Ali idućeg dana sam poslao email sa svojom ostavkom.

744
00:48:13,950 --> 00:48:16,350
[SPEAKER_00] And I honestly didn't know if I'd ever be in ministry again.

745
00:48:16,830 --> 00:48:19,530
[SPEAKER_01] I nisam bio siguran da li ću se ikad više vratiti služenju.

746
00:48:19,890 --> 00:48:22,830
[SPEAKER_00] But after I sent that email, that's when I started coming to the couch.

747
00:48:23,430 --> 00:48:27,030
[SPEAKER_01] Ali kad sam poslao taj email, taj dan sam počeo se pojavljivati na kauču.

748
00:48:27,570 --> 00:48:30,150
[SPEAKER_00] And when I told my wife about sending that email,

749
00:48:31,650 --> 00:48:34,290
[SPEAKER_00] she wasn't overjoyed, but it was something very subtle.

750
00:48:35,310 --> 00:48:42,450
[SPEAKER_01] Kad sam ženi rekao da sam poslao taj email, ona nije bila nešto previše radosna, nego je bila puno, puno

751
00:48:44,910 --> 00:48:45,450
[SPEAKER_01] suptilnija.

752
00:48:45,810 --> 00:48:47,310
[SPEAKER_00] Yes. Something in her softened.

753
00:48:47,790 --> 00:48:49,410
[SPEAKER_01] Nešto u njoj je omekšalo.

754
00:48:50,070 --> 00:48:54,930
[SPEAKER_00] Like that lie of me loving ministry more than her. It's like that layer broke off.

755
00:48:55,170 --> 00:49:00,390
[SPEAKER_01] Kao da je ta laž da volim služenje više od nje, kao da se odvalila.

756
00:49:01,170 --> 00:49:05,970
[SPEAKER_00] And the next months of coming to the couch, we saw so much restoration happen there.

757
00:49:06,630 --> 00:49:13,290
[SPEAKER_01] I u idućim mjesecima i u dolascima na taj kauč, vidjeli smo jako puno obnove u odnosu koja se dogodila.

758
00:49:14,610 --> 00:49:19,050
[SPEAKER_00] Now, if that's your struggle, I can't promise you the same journey that Rose and I have had.

759
00:49:19,770 --> 00:49:25,830
[SPEAKER_01] Ako imate sličnu borbu, ne mogu vam obećati da trebate ići istim putem kojim smo Rose i ja išli.

760
00:49:27,030 --> 00:49:27,330
[SPEAKER_01] Ruža.

761
00:49:33,210 --> 00:49:36,030
[SPEAKER_00] But I'm going to say, if you make that choice, it's totally worth it.

762
00:49:36,390 --> 00:49:42,930
[SPEAKER_01] Ali ako odlučite napraviti taj odabir, u potpunosti je vrijedan toga.

763
00:49:43,110 --> 00:49:44,850
[SPEAKER_00] Because Jesus makes all things new.

764
00:49:45,210 --> 00:49:47,730
[SPEAKER_01] Jer Isus sve stvara novo, sve čini novo.

765
00:49:48,030 --> 00:49:51,090
[SPEAKER_00] In fact, do you want to know who recommended Encounter Ministries to me?

766
00:49:51,570 --> 00:49:53,970
[SPEAKER_01] Što mislite, tko mi je predložio Encounter Ministries?

767
00:49:54,330 --> 00:49:55,050
[SPEAKER_00] Surprise!

768
00:49:55,230 --> 00:49:55,950
[SPEAKER_01] Iznenađenje!

769
00:49:56,670 --> 00:49:57,270
[SPEAKER_00] It's my wife.

770
00:49:57,450 --> 00:49:57,810
[SPEAKER_01] Moja žena.

771
00:49:57,930 --> 00:50:05,190
[SPEAKER_00] It's my wife. And I'd go on to see more miracles with Encounter than I'd ever seen in my 10-plus years of ministry combined.

772
00:50:05,550 --> 00:50:11,970
[SPEAKER_01] I u Encounteru sam u kratko vrijeme vidio puno više čudesa i milosti nego u 10 godina služenja prije.

773
00:50:12,270 --> 00:50:14,010
[SPEAKER_00] But now she was with me in it.

774
00:50:14,190 --> 00:50:15,990
[SPEAKER_01] Ali ona je sad bila sa mnom u tome.

775
00:50:16,410 --> 00:50:17,070
[SPEAKER_00] Love is patient.

776
00:50:17,550 --> 00:50:18,450
[SPEAKER_01] Ljubav je strpljiva.

777
00:50:19,290 --> 00:50:20,370
[SPEAKER_00] Let's move to the next one.

778
00:50:20,490 --> 00:50:21,030
[SPEAKER_01] Idemo dalje.

779
00:50:22,050 --> 00:50:24,090
[SPEAKER_00] Love is kind. It is not rude.

780
00:50:24,330 --> 00:50:30,210
[SPEAKER_01] Ljubav je nježna. Nije... Nije nepristojna.

781
00:50:31,830 --> 00:50:37,830
[SPEAKER_01] Dobrostiva. We have very different translations.

782
00:50:37,950 --> 00:50:42,150
[SPEAKER_00] Oh, really? Yours is probably right.

783
00:50:44,490 --> 00:50:50,010
[SPEAKER_00] So go ahead and declare this: "I am kind."

784
00:50:53,550 --> 00:50:58,530
[SPEAKER_01] Ja sam dobrostiv. Ja sam dobrostiv.

785
00:51:00,690 --> 00:51:01,590
[SPEAKER_00] I am not rude.

786
00:51:03,570 --> 00:51:06,390
[SPEAKER_01] Nisam bezobrazan, nepristojan.

787
00:51:07,410 --> 00:51:11,610
[SPEAKER_00] Just pay attention to how that feels coming out of your mouth: "I am kind, I am not

788
00:51:11,670 --> 00:51:14,130
[SPEAKER_01] rude." Gledajte kako zvuči kad izlazi iz vaših usta.

789
00:51:20,310 --> 00:51:24,690
[SPEAKER_00] I think one of the most memorable passages in the Bible on rudeness.

790
00:51:24,930 --> 00:51:28,290
[SPEAKER_01] Jedan od najboljih citata o

791
00:51:30,390 --> 00:51:31,290
[SPEAKER_01] nepristojnosti.

792
00:51:32,070 --> 00:51:33,690
[SPEAKER_00] Is in 2 Kings chapter 2.

793
00:51:33,870 --> 00:51:37,230
[SPEAKER_01] I u 2. Kraljevima, 2. poglavlje.

794
00:51:37,590 --> 00:51:38,490
[SPEAKER_00] I'll paraphrase it.

795
00:51:38,850 --> 00:51:39,690
[SPEAKER_01] Parafrazirat ću.

796
00:51:40,710 --> 00:51:41,850
[SPEAKER_00] So we have Elisha.

797
00:51:42,270 --> 00:51:43,170
[SPEAKER_01] Imamo Elizeja.

798
00:51:43,410 --> 00:51:45,570
[SPEAKER_00] Who just received a double portion from Elijah.

799
00:51:45,810 --> 00:51:49,350
[SPEAKER_01] Koji je primio duplu porciju pomazanja i Duha i Linog.

800
00:51:49,530 --> 00:51:54,090
[SPEAKER_00] And then immediately he goes and miraculously purifies an entire city's water supply.

801
00:51:54,570 --> 00:51:56,670
[SPEAKER_01] I odlazi i na čudesan način

802
00:51:58,290 --> 00:52:02,010
[SPEAKER_01] očišćuje, dovodi vode za cijeli grad.

803
00:52:02,310 --> 00:52:03,570
[SPEAKER_00] Which is super awesome, right?

804
00:52:03,870 --> 00:52:05,430
[SPEAKER_01] To je vrhunski, ono, čudesno.

805
00:52:06,390 --> 00:52:07,470
[SPEAKER_00] Nobody thinks that's awesome.

806
00:52:07,650 --> 00:52:08,850
[SPEAKER_01] Nitko ne misli da je to čudesno.

807
00:52:10,110 --> 00:52:14,130
[SPEAKER_00] Okay. Well, it says, "From there, Elisha went up to Bethel."

808
00:52:14,490 --> 00:52:18,390
[SPEAKER_01] Kaže da je odande Elizej otišao u Betel.

809
00:52:18,810 --> 00:52:22,530
[SPEAKER_00] While he was on the way, some little boys came out of the city and jeered at him.

810
00:52:23,430 --> 00:52:30,930
[SPEAKER_01] I dok je išao prema gore, neki dječaci su izašli iz grada i počeli su ga... počeli su ga provocirati.

811
00:52:31,170 --> 00:52:33,990
[SPEAKER_00] They said, "Go away, Baldi! Go away, Baldi!"

812
00:52:34,050 --> 00:52:36,750
[SPEAKER_01] Govorili su mu: "Odi ćelavi, bježi ćelavi!"

813
00:52:37,890 --> 00:52:41,490
[SPEAKER_00] The prophet turned and saw them, and he cursed them in the name of the Lord.

814
00:52:41,970 --> 00:52:47,670
[SPEAKER_01] Prorok ih je vidio, okrenuo im se i prokleo ih u ime Isusovo, u ime Gospodnje.

815
00:52:48,510 --> 00:52:52,590
[SPEAKER_00] Then two shebears came out of the woods and tore 42 of the children to pieces.

816
00:52:53,670 --> 00:52:58,950
[SPEAKER_01] Onda su izašla 2 medvjeda i 42 djece, rasturila u komade.

817
00:52:59,550 --> 00:53:00,390
[SPEAKER_00] The word of the Lord.

818
00:53:00,810 --> 00:53:01,590
[SPEAKER_01] Riječ Gospodnja.

819
00:53:02,670 --> 00:53:06,150
[SPEAKER_00] Now, I don't know if Elisha was insecure about his hair loss.

820
00:53:06,450 --> 00:53:10,350
[SPEAKER_01] Nisam siguran da je Elizej bio baš nesiguran oko gubitka svoje kose.

821
00:53:11,010 --> 00:53:14,910
[SPEAKER_00] But it seems clear to me that the Lord does not like rudeness to the ones he loves.

822
00:53:16,110 --> 00:53:20,370
[SPEAKER_01] Ali siguran sam da Gospodin ne voli nepristojnost prema onima koje ljubi.

823
00:53:20,790 --> 00:53:25,290
[SPEAKER_00] Maybe this might also cause us to pause before we criticize how our spouse looks.

824
00:53:25,830 --> 00:53:33,690
[SPEAKER_01] Možda će nas ovo natjerati da se zaustavimo i pauziramo prije nego što kritiziramo svoje supružnike o tome kako izgledaju.

825
00:53:34,290 --> 00:53:36,930
[SPEAKER_00] But when we talk about kindness, we're talking about honor.

826
00:53:37,410 --> 00:53:41,070
[SPEAKER_01] Ali kad pričamo o nježnosti i dobrostivosti, pričamo o časti.

827
00:53:41,250 --> 00:53:44,670
[SPEAKER_00] Am I treating someone with the dignity that God has given them?

828
00:53:45,030 --> 00:53:50,970
[SPEAKER_01] Da li se odnosim prema nekome sa čašću i dostojanstvom koje je Gospodin dao toj osobi?

829
00:53:51,450 --> 00:53:53,490
[SPEAKER_00] Especially in the middle of disagreement.

830
00:53:54,030 --> 00:53:55,770
[SPEAKER_01] Posebice usred svađe.

831
00:53:56,010 --> 00:54:01,050
[SPEAKER_00] When maybe the dinner table feels like the table the Lord has set before you in front of your enemies.

832
00:54:02,250 --> 00:54:04,470
[SPEAKER_01] I kad se naš stol

833
00:54:05,670 --> 00:54:10,170
[SPEAKER_01] u blagovaonici čini kao stol koji je Gospodin postavio između tebe i tvog neprijatelja.

834
00:54:11,130 --> 00:54:14,610
[SPEAKER_00] Because sometimes in the middle of their brokenness, you don't see their dignity.

835
00:54:15,090 --> 00:54:20,310
[SPEAKER_01] Jer nekad usred toga da vidimo njihovu slomljenost, ne vidimo njihovo dostojanstvo.

836
00:54:20,490 --> 00:54:23,370
[SPEAKER_00] And you have to turn and ask God for His perspective.

837
00:54:23,730 --> 00:54:26,790
[SPEAKER_01] I moraš moliti Gospodina da ti pokaže Njegovu perspektivu.

838
00:54:27,330 --> 00:54:28,710
[SPEAKER_00] This is the way that I do this.

839
00:54:29,070 --> 00:54:30,510
[SPEAKER_01] Ovo je način na koji sam ja činio.

840
00:54:30,810 --> 00:54:35,670
[SPEAKER_00] I ask God, "Help me to see my spouse first as your beloved child."

841
00:54:36,990 --> 00:54:43,110
[SPEAKER_01] Molio sam Gospodina da mi da da vidim svoju suprugu kao Njegovo ljubljeno dijete.

842
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:48,990
[SPEAKER_00] Then once I see that, I say, "Help me to see them walking in the full security of your love."

843
00:54:49,410 --> 00:54:55,830
[SPEAKER_01] A onda bih molio da mi pokaže, kad bi to vidio: "Daj mi da ju vidim kako hoda u punoj sigurnosti Tvoje ljubavi."

844
00:54:56,130 --> 00:55:02,610
[SPEAKER_00] And then when I see that, I say, "Help me to see them walking in the fullness of the gifting that You've put over their life."

845
00:55:02,910 --> 00:55:09,930
[SPEAKER_01] A kada bih to vidio, onda bih zamolio da mi Gospodin pokaže kako izgledaju u punini darova koje im je, koje joj je dao.

846
00:55:11,370 --> 00:55:14,970
[SPEAKER_00] Whenever I do this and I see how God sees my wife.

847
00:55:15,030 --> 00:55:18,450
[SPEAKER_01] Kada god bih to učinio i vidio kako Gospodin gleda moju suprugu.

848
00:55:19,170 --> 00:55:23,850
[SPEAKER_00] No matter how rude or indifferent she is to me.

849
00:55:24,270 --> 00:55:26,790
[SPEAKER_01] Bez obzira koliko bila možda nepristojna ili

850
00:55:28,230 --> 00:55:29,310
[SPEAKER_01] ravnodušna prema meni.

851
00:55:30,210 --> 00:55:33,510
[SPEAKER_00] Which I am as well to her. Okay, let's be fair.

852
00:55:33,750 --> 00:55:36,210
[SPEAKER_01] Kao što bih ja nekad bio prema njoj, ako ćemo biti fer.

853
00:55:36,450 --> 00:55:39,150
[SPEAKER_00] But when I see that vision, I fall in love with her all over again.

854
00:55:39,270 --> 00:55:41,790
[SPEAKER_01] Ali kad bih vidio tu viziju, opet bih se zaljubio u nju.

855
00:55:43,050 --> 00:55:47,250
[SPEAKER_00] I've told people, when my wife finally walks in her full authority.

856
00:55:47,850 --> 00:55:52,050
[SPEAKER_01] Rekao sam ljudima: "Kad moja žena bude hodala u svom punom autoritetu."

857
00:55:52,350 --> 00:55:55,650
[SPEAKER_00] I've seen, prophetically, she has more power than I have.

858
00:55:56,010 --> 00:55:58,050
[SPEAKER_01] Proročki sam vidio da je snažnija od mene.

859
00:55:58,170 --> 00:55:58,890
[SPEAKER_00] And I get jealous.

860
00:55:59,490 --> 00:56:00,330
[SPEAKER_01] Bio sam ljubomoran.

861
00:56:01,110 --> 00:56:05,190
[SPEAKER_00] And I think when we've discussed it, she's doing the same for me.

862
00:56:05,910 --> 00:56:09,510
[SPEAKER_01] I mislim da kad smo raspravljali o tome, ona isto tako mene vidi.

863
00:56:09,690 --> 00:56:11,790
[SPEAKER_00] She sees the same vision, but towards me.

864
00:56:12,270 --> 00:56:13,950
[SPEAKER_01] Istu viziju ima za mene.

865
00:56:14,670 --> 00:56:17,910
[SPEAKER_00] Seeing the Father's vision is so powerful for your spouse.

866
00:56:18,390 --> 00:56:23,730
[SPEAKER_01] Vidjeti Očev pogled i Očevu viziju o svojoj supruzi je jako snažno.

867
00:56:24,930 --> 00:56:26,010
[SPEAKER_00] Let's move to the next one.

868
00:56:26,610 --> 00:56:27,270
[SPEAKER_01] Idemo dalje.

869
00:56:27,570 --> 00:56:28,530
[SPEAKER_00] Love is not jealous.

870
00:56:29,190 --> 00:56:30,690
[SPEAKER_01] Ljubav ne zavidi.

871
00:56:30,990 --> 00:56:32,610
[SPEAKER_00] It does not seek its own interests.

872
00:56:33,030 --> 00:56:33,810
[SPEAKER_01] Ne traži svoje.

873
00:56:34,350 --> 00:56:38,430
[SPEAKER_00] Go ahead and declare this after Him: "I am not jealous."

874
00:56:39,630 --> 00:56:42,690
[SPEAKER_01] Proklamirajte ovo: "Ja ne zavidim."

875
00:56:44,370 --> 00:56:45,750
[SPEAKER_00] I don't seek my own interests.

876
00:56:46,170 --> 00:56:47,250
[SPEAKER_01] I ne tražim svoje.

877
00:56:50,670 --> 00:56:51,870
[SPEAKER_00] Pay attention to how that feels.

878
00:56:52,470 --> 00:56:55,170
[SPEAKER_01] Pogledajte kako to odzvanja u vašim srcima.

879
00:57:07,710 --> 00:57:09,210
[SPEAKER_00] For myself, I'll make a confession.

880
00:57:11,430 --> 00:57:12,570
[SPEAKER_01] Ispovijedat ću sebe.

881
00:57:13,050 --> 00:57:15,330
[SPEAKER_00] I'm an American, we seek our own interests.

882
00:57:15,510 --> 00:57:18,150
[SPEAKER_01] Ja sam Amerikanac i mi tražimo svoje.

883
00:57:20,670 --> 00:57:26,610
[SPEAKER_00] Statistically, we are 4% of the world's population, yet we account for one-third of the world's spending.

884
00:57:27,030 --> 00:57:34,170
[SPEAKER_01] Statistički, mi smo 4% svjetske populacije, a trošimo 1/3 svjetske potrošnje.

885
00:57:34,950 --> 00:57:38,550
[SPEAKER_00] Here's another confession: I'm the youngest sibling. Is anybody else in here?

886
00:57:38,730 --> 00:57:43,710
[SPEAKER_01] Još jedno priznanje: ja sam najmlađi od braće i sestara. Ima još netko?

887
00:57:44,130 --> 00:57:46,530
[SPEAKER_00] Here it is: we're a little self-absorbed.

888
00:57:47,310 --> 00:57:48,630
[SPEAKER_01] Mi smo malo puni sebe.

889
00:57:49,890 --> 00:57:52,050
[SPEAKER_00] Now, oldest siblings, chill out for a second.

890
00:57:52,350 --> 00:57:53,850
[SPEAKER_01] Svi ostali, samo se smirite.

891
00:57:53,970 --> 00:57:56,310
[SPEAKER_00] You don't have to agree with that so enthusiastically.

892
00:57:56,550 --> 00:57:59,370
[SPEAKER_01] Ne morate se tako entuzijastično s nama složiti oko toga.

893
00:57:59,910 --> 00:58:01,710
[SPEAKER_00] Now, why are we so self-absorbed?

894
00:58:02,010 --> 00:58:03,150
[SPEAKER_01] Zašto smo puni sebe?

895
00:58:03,330 --> 00:58:05,850
[SPEAKER_00] Because just most of the time, we didn't have to care for someone.

896
00:58:06,270 --> 00:58:08,850
[SPEAKER_01] Jer većinu vremena nismo morali brinuti o nikome drugome.

897
00:58:09,030 --> 00:58:11,010
[SPEAKER_00] It's not our fault that mom stopped having kids.

898
00:58:11,190 --> 00:58:13,530
[SPEAKER_01] Nije naša krivica što je mama prestala imati djecu.

899
00:58:15,810 --> 00:58:20,910
[SPEAKER_00] In 2019, my wife and I, we went on a Healing the Whole Person conference with Dr. Bob.

900
00:58:21,150 --> 00:58:25,830
[SPEAKER_01] 2019. išli smo na konferenciju Iscjeljenje cijele osobe, dr. Boba Schutza.

901
00:58:26,130 --> 00:58:33,330
[SPEAKER_00] And some of you are aware that Dr. Bob, he outlines the 7 deadly sins and adds on the 7 deadly wounds.

902
00:58:34,830 --> 00:58:39,750
[SPEAKER_01] Neki od vas znaju da dr. Bob priča o 7 smrtnih grijeha i 7 smrtnih rana.

903
00:58:40,410 --> 00:58:44,310
[SPEAKER_00] One of the deadly sins I was surprised to connect with was greed.

904
00:58:45,090 --> 00:58:50,010
[SPEAKER_01] Jedan od 7 glavnih grijeha s kojima sam se vidio da sam povezan je pohlepa.

905
00:58:50,430 --> 00:58:53,850
[SPEAKER_00] Now, I never thought that was my problem, because we didn't have much money growing up.

906
00:58:54,030 --> 00:58:57,750
[SPEAKER_01] Nikad nisam mislio da je to moj problem jer nismo imali puno novca dok sam odrastao.

907
00:58:58,590 --> 00:59:03,270
[SPEAKER_00] But I found it interesting to hear him say greed is actually an attachment to security.

908
00:59:04,170 --> 00:59:09,030
[SPEAKER_01] Ono što me iznenadilo je kad je rekao da je pohlepa navezanost na sigurnost.

909
00:59:09,330 --> 00:59:13,230
[SPEAKER_00] Like, instead of turning to God as your provider, you turn to stuff.

910
00:59:13,650 --> 00:59:18,090
[SPEAKER_01] Umjesto da se osloniš na Boga koji proviđa, oslanjaš se na stvari, na materijalno.

911
00:59:18,690 --> 00:59:25,050
[SPEAKER_00] So in my family, as we amassed all this cheap stuff that we didn't need, it was actually sinful.

912
00:59:25,530 --> 00:59:33,030
[SPEAKER_01] I kao obitelj, dok smo se natrpavali jeftinim stvarima koje nam nisu bile potrebne, to je u stvari bilo grešno ponašanje.

913
00:59:33,690 --> 00:59:36,330
[SPEAKER_00] I got convicted of this months later.

914
00:59:36,750 --> 00:59:39,210
[SPEAKER_01] Poslije mi se to pokazalo, nakon nekoliko mjeseci.

915
00:59:39,450 --> 00:59:44,130
[SPEAKER_00] When I found a pair of shoes for me on eBay for $9, free shipping.

916
00:59:44,610 --> 00:59:50,430
[SPEAKER_01] Kad sam na eBayu pronašao tenisice, moj broj, za 9 dolara na eBayu, bez poštarine.

917
00:59:50,730 --> 00:59:52,110
[SPEAKER_00] That's cheaper than 9 euros.

918
00:59:52,470 --> 00:59:53,850
[SPEAKER_01] To je jeftinije nego 9 eura.

919
00:59:54,870 --> 00:59:56,850
[SPEAKER_00] So I place that order, and then what do I see?

920
00:59:57,570 --> 01:00:00,630
[SPEAKER_01] I naručio sam te tenisice, i što sam poslije toga vidio?

921
01:00:01,050 --> 01:00:04,710
[SPEAKER_00] The same seller selling another pair for $5, free shipping.

922
01:00:05,130 --> 01:00:09,510
[SPEAKER_01] Isti čovjek prodaje još jedan par za 5 dolara, isto bez poštarine.

923
01:00:09,690 --> 01:00:12,090
[SPEAKER_00] And two others for $1, free shipping.

924
01:00:12,450 --> 01:00:15,030
[SPEAKER_01] I još dvoje za po 1 dolar, bez poštarine.

925
01:00:15,210 --> 01:00:17,190
[SPEAKER_00] So what did I do without asking my wife?

926
01:00:17,490 --> 01:00:19,170
[SPEAKER_01] Što sam napravio bez da sam pitao ženu?

927
01:00:19,290 --> 01:00:20,130
[SPEAKER_00] I bought them all.

928
01:00:20,550 --> 01:00:21,390
[SPEAKER_01] Sve sam ih kupio.

929
01:00:22,530 --> 01:00:24,330
[SPEAKER_00] And I know what you're thinking, but you're wrong.

930
01:00:24,510 --> 01:00:26,070
[SPEAKER_01] Znam što mislite i u krivu ste.

931
01:00:26,310 --> 01:00:27,090
[SPEAKER_00] They did arrive.

932
01:00:27,450 --> 01:00:28,170
[SPEAKER_01] One su došle.

933
01:00:28,590 --> 01:00:29,790
[SPEAKER_00] In this giant box.

934
01:00:30,210 --> 01:00:31,170
[SPEAKER_01] U ogromnoj kutiji.

935
01:00:31,350 --> 01:00:35,310
[SPEAKER_00] I brought it into my house. It was taped up. I pulled back the tape.

936
01:00:36,030 --> 01:00:40,410
[SPEAKER_01] Unio sam u kuću cijelu kutiju, bile su zalijepljene, otrgnuo sam traku.

937
01:00:40,710 --> 01:00:45,270
[SPEAKER_00] I open it up and there's a sign on top that says "Free Gift."

938
01:00:45,810 --> 01:00:49,650
[SPEAKER_01] Otvorio sam kutiju i unutra je bilo: "Znak: besplatni dar."

939
01:00:50,250 --> 01:00:57,030
[SPEAKER_00] And inside, I'm counting: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8.

940
01:00:57,270 --> 01:01:00,090
[SPEAKER_01] Izbrojao sam 8 parova cipela.

941
01:01:00,630 --> 01:01:06,570
[SPEAKER_00] In addition to the 4 pairs of shoes that I ordered, are 4 additional pairs of shoes in this box.

942
01:01:06,810 --> 01:01:09,690
[SPEAKER_01] Uz 4 koje sam naručio i još 4 besplatna para.

943
01:01:10,470 --> 01:01:18,510
[SPEAKER_00] Now, part of me was really creeped out. Like, I was expecting, like, this package will self-destruct in 3, 2, 1.

944
01:01:20,070 --> 01:01:27,450
[SPEAKER_01] Dio mene je bio malo i uznemiren, mislio sam da će uskoro početi zvuk: "Ovaj paket će eksplodirati za 3, 2, 1."

945
01:01:28,710 --> 01:01:36,210
[SPEAKER_00] But I remember in that moment, I just turned to the Lord and I was like, "Lord, I don't need any of these shoes."

946
01:01:36,750 --> 01:01:42,030
[SPEAKER_01] Ali u tom trenutku sam se okrenuo i progovorio Bogu: "Gospodine, ne trebam nijednu od ovih cipela."

947
01:01:42,510 --> 01:01:46,770
[SPEAKER_00] It was like St. Paul says in Romans, the kindness of God leads to repentance.

948
01:01:47,130 --> 01:01:53,070
[SPEAKER_01] Kad Pavao kaže: "Božja dobrota vodi prema pokajanju."

949
01:01:53,250 --> 01:01:56,310
[SPEAKER_00] And I was so convicted that I actually ended up giving all the shoes away.

950
01:01:56,610 --> 01:01:59,490
[SPEAKER_01] Bio sam toliko uvjeren da sam sve cipele podijelio.

951
01:01:59,850 --> 01:02:12,030
[SPEAKER_00] And that conviction stayed with me. I found myself going to the store, and if there were 2 items of the same item, but one was on sale and one was not, I would end up buying the more expensive item.

952
01:02:12,570 --> 01:02:20,370
[SPEAKER_01] Bio sam toliko uvjeren u to da kad bih otišao u dućan i našao 2 artikla koja su ista, jedan koji je na popustu, drugi koji nije, kupio bih onaj koji nije na popustu.

953
01:02:20,910 --> 01:02:22,470
[SPEAKER_00] Not because it was a better product.

954
01:02:22,770 --> 01:02:24,270
[SPEAKER_01] Ne zato što je to bio bolji proizvod.

955
01:02:24,570 --> 01:02:27,570
[SPEAKER_00] But because I wanted to break the power that greed had over me.

956
01:02:27,750 --> 01:02:32,010
[SPEAKER_01] Nego zato što sam želio slomiti moć pohlepe koju je imala nada mnom.

957
01:02:32,310 --> 01:02:36,690
[SPEAKER_00] And I wanted to respond to something that the Lord told me years earlier that I want to share with you.

958
01:02:37,050 --> 01:02:41,610
[SPEAKER_01] I želio sam odgovoriti na nešto što mi je Gospodin progovorio godinama ranije, što ću podijeliti s vama.

959
01:02:41,910 --> 01:02:45,090
[SPEAKER_00] When I first met my wife, it was in a young adult prayer group.

960
01:02:45,270 --> 01:02:47,370
[SPEAKER_01] Kada sam upoznao svoju suprugu, bilo je to u

961
01:02:49,530 --> 01:02:51,330
[SPEAKER_01] jednoj molitvenoj grupi mladih.

962
01:02:51,630 --> 01:02:54,090
[SPEAKER_00] And most of it was really good. We prayed with each other.

963
01:02:54,330 --> 01:02:56,670
[SPEAKER_01] Većinom je bilo jako dobro, molili smo jedni za druge.

964
01:02:57,450 --> 01:03:01,410
[SPEAKER_00] But we also discovered, in this small group of 7 or 8 of us.

965
01:03:01,530 --> 01:03:04,770
[SPEAKER_01] Ali smo otkrili da u malim grupama od nas 7 ili 8.

966
01:03:04,950 --> 01:03:08,490
[SPEAKER_00] Whenever prayer would get heightened, like very anointed.

967
01:03:08,910 --> 01:03:11,010
[SPEAKER_01] Kad bi molitva postala jako pomazana.

968
01:03:11,610 --> 01:03:18,750
[SPEAKER_00] About half of the ladies, including my wife Rose, would end up on the floor writhing in what we discerned were demonic manifestations.

969
01:03:20,010 --> 01:03:27,210
[SPEAKER_01] Polovica djevojaka, među kojima i moja žena, bi završile na podu i imale nešto što smo mi nazvali demonološke reakcije.

970
01:03:27,570 --> 01:03:34,590
[SPEAKER_00] And the leaders would make sure they were safe, but essentially it was just waiting it out, nothing resolved, and it was happening every week.

971
01:03:35,310 --> 01:03:45,990
[SPEAKER_01] I voditelji su uvijek pazili da one budu na sigurnom i da sve bude dobro, ali kako su tjedni prolazili, ništa se nije mijenjalo i sve se događalo iznova i iznova.

972
01:03:46,230 --> 01:03:49,890
[SPEAKER_00] And I remember driving home one day, just crying out to the Lord.

973
01:03:50,010 --> 01:03:54,450
[SPEAKER_01] Sjećam se dok sam se vozio jednog dana doma i molio, vapio Bogu.

974
01:03:55,110 --> 01:03:58,470
[SPEAKER_00] And I said, "Lord, what will it take to get our sisters free?"

975
01:03:58,830 --> 01:04:04,770
[SPEAKER_01] I pitao sam ga: "Gospodine, što je potrebno da naše sestre budu oslobođene?"

976
01:04:05,070 --> 01:04:09,150
[SPEAKER_00] And what I heard back surprised me. It was as clear as day. I heard detachment.

977
01:04:09,510 --> 01:04:16,950
[SPEAKER_01] Ono što sam čuo i što me jako pogodilo je nenavezanost. Odgovor je bio nenavezanost.

978
01:04:17,430 --> 01:04:20,790
[SPEAKER_00] And a response came right out of me, and immediately I said, "No."

979
01:04:21,390 --> 01:04:24,930
[SPEAKER_01] I odmah iz mene je izletio odgovor koji je bio: "Ne."

980
01:04:25,830 --> 01:04:30,690
[SPEAKER_00] Because it was like God was telling me, "Kevin, if you want to take on the enemy."

981
01:04:31,410 --> 01:04:35,670
[SPEAKER_01] Jer mi je Gospodin govorio: "Kevine, ako se želiš boriti protiv neprijatelja."

982
01:04:36,210 --> 01:04:38,610
[SPEAKER_00] You can't be divided. He'll use that against you.

983
01:04:38,850 --> 01:04:41,610
[SPEAKER_01] Ne možeš biti podijeljen, iskoristit će to protiv tebe.

984
01:04:42,210 --> 01:04:45,510
[SPEAKER_00] And in that moment, I knew I was attached to so many things.

985
01:04:45,750 --> 01:04:50,310
[SPEAKER_01] I u tom trenutku sam automatski znao da sam navezan na toliko puno stvari.

986
01:04:50,850 --> 01:04:51,270
[SPEAKER_00] Movies.

987
01:04:52,050 --> 01:04:52,530
[SPEAKER_01] Filmovi.

988
01:04:52,770 --> 01:04:53,250
[SPEAKER_00] Music.

989
01:04:53,610 --> 01:04:54,030
[SPEAKER_01] Glazba.

990
01:04:54,330 --> 01:04:54,750
[SPEAKER_00] Shopping.

991
01:04:55,530 --> 01:04:56,250
[SPEAKER_01] Šopingiranje.

992
01:04:56,430 --> 01:04:56,910
[SPEAKER_00] Drinking.

993
01:04:58,050 --> 01:04:58,410
[SPEAKER_01] Pijenje.

994
01:04:59,310 --> 01:05:02,610
[SPEAKER_00] And I wasn't willing, I wasn't ready to let those things go.

995
01:05:02,850 --> 01:05:05,130
[SPEAKER_01] I nisam bio spreman otpustiti te stvari.

996
01:05:05,550 --> 01:05:08,190
[SPEAKER_00] I was serving two masters, God and mammon.

997
01:05:08,850 --> 01:05:12,210
[SPEAKER_01] Služio sam dvojici gospodara, Bogu i bogatstvu.

998
01:05:12,570 --> 01:05:16,770
[SPEAKER_00] So as I headed into marriage, I was still very attached to many things.

999
01:05:16,950 --> 01:05:20,310
[SPEAKER_01] Kako sam ulazio u brak, i dalje sam bio jako navezan na mnogo stvari.

1000
01:05:20,850 --> 01:05:22,350
[SPEAKER_00] I want to talk about entertainment.

1001
01:05:22,530 --> 01:05:24,450
[SPEAKER_01] Želim razgovarati o zabavi.

1002
01:05:24,630 --> 01:05:25,410
[SPEAKER_00] I love movies.

1003
01:05:25,770 --> 01:05:26,490
[SPEAKER_01] Volim filmove.

1004
01:05:26,850 --> 01:05:30,330
[SPEAKER_00] Growing up, it was a very sheltered home. We didn't get to watch a lot of movies.

1005
01:05:30,930 --> 01:05:35,190
[SPEAKER_01] Dok sam odrastao, bili smo u jako zatvorenom kućanstvu, nismo gledali puno filmova.

1006
01:05:35,730 --> 01:05:37,110
[SPEAKER_00] But now I'm an adult.

1007
01:05:37,410 --> 01:05:38,370
[SPEAKER_01] Sada sam odrastao.

1008
01:05:38,970 --> 01:05:40,530
[SPEAKER_00] So I could watch whatever I wanted.

1009
01:05:40,890 --> 01:05:42,210
[SPEAKER_01] Mogu gledati što god želim.

1010
01:05:42,330 --> 01:05:45,450
[SPEAKER_00] I remember going to the pawn shop. They had $2 DVDs.

1011
01:05:46,650 --> 01:05:50,970
[SPEAKER_01] Sjećam se da sam išao u zalagaonicu, imali su filmove za 2 dolara.

1012
01:05:51,150 --> 01:05:54,510
[SPEAKER_00] So I built this huge collection, hundreds of movies.

1013
01:05:54,750 --> 01:05:57,330
[SPEAKER_01] Imao sam ovu ogromnu kolekciju sa stotinama filmova.

1014
01:05:57,630 --> 01:05:59,970
[SPEAKER_00] Same with music, massive collection of

1015
01:06:00,330 --> 01:06:02,070
[SPEAKER_01] music. Isto sa glazbom, ogromna kolekcija.

1016
01:06:02,250 --> 01:06:03,270
[SPEAKER_00] And it was all secular.

1017
01:06:03,510 --> 01:06:04,950
[SPEAKER_01] I sve je bilo svjetovno.

1018
01:06:05,610 --> 01:06:08,190
[SPEAKER_00] Now, with all of these voices, with all of this content.

1019
01:06:08,670 --> 01:06:11,190
[SPEAKER_01] Sa svim tim glasovima i svim tim sadržajem.

1020
01:06:11,970 --> 01:06:15,330
[SPEAKER_00] How much of this environment do you think was holy?

1021
01:06:15,510 --> 01:06:17,610
[SPEAKER_01] Koliko tog okruženja je bilo sveto?

1022
01:06:18,870 --> 01:06:22,950
[SPEAKER_00] I actually began to see, when I would put on something of darker nature.

1023
01:06:23,070 --> 01:06:26,490
[SPEAKER_01] Kad bih stavio nešto tamnije naravi, mračnije naravi.

1024
01:06:27,030 --> 01:06:30,510
[SPEAKER_00] Like, say a movie, the darkness of that movie that I put on.

1025
01:06:30,630 --> 01:06:32,670
[SPEAKER_01] Kad bih stavio film neki koji je bio mračniji,

1026
01:06:34,350 --> 01:06:36,750
[SPEAKER_01] mrak tog filma, tama tog filma.

1027
01:06:36,930 --> 01:06:41,730
[SPEAKER_00] Yeah, it would linger in my home, primarily with my wife.

1028
01:06:42,090 --> 01:06:46,290
[SPEAKER_01] Kao da bi se uvukla u naš dom, prvenstveno s mojom ženom.

1029
01:06:46,710 --> 01:06:53,250
[SPEAKER_00] Almost every time she would have these nightmares or night terrors, and she'd get angry with me for having her watch it with me.

1030
01:06:53,970 --> 01:07:01,290
[SPEAKER_01] I gotovo uvijek bi imala noćne more i noćne napadaje, i bila bi ljuta na mene zato što sam ju nagovorio da gleda sama.

1031
01:07:02,010 --> 01:07:04,350
[SPEAKER_00] So as I started to enter into healing ministry.

1032
01:07:04,770 --> 01:07:07,110
[SPEAKER_01] Kako sam počeo ulaziti u službu ozdravljanja.

1033
01:07:07,410 --> 01:07:08,910
[SPEAKER_00] I felt the Lord telling me this.

1034
01:07:09,150 --> 01:07:11,130
[SPEAKER_01] Osjetio sam kao da mi Gospodin govori ovo.

1035
01:07:11,430 --> 01:07:16,290
[SPEAKER_00] He said, "Kevin, what you keep will sow roots in your home."

1036
01:07:17,130 --> 01:07:23,730
[SPEAKER_01] I rekao mi je: "Kevine, što zadržiš, posijat će sjemenje i pustiti korijenje u tvome domu."

1037
01:07:24,090 --> 01:07:28,050
[SPEAKER_00] So one day I went through each of the hundreds of movies I had.

1038
01:07:28,230 --> 01:07:30,810
[SPEAKER_01] I jednog dana sam prošao kroz stotine filmova koje imam.

1039
01:07:31,290 --> 01:07:37,530
[SPEAKER_00] I picked it up and I discerned one: does this leave me feeling upbuilt, encouraged, and consoled?

1040
01:07:39,330 --> 01:07:45,210
[SPEAKER_01] Da li me ovo ostavlja nakon što pogledam uzdignutim, ohrabrenim, utješenim?

1041
01:07:45,630 --> 01:07:48,210
[SPEAKER_00] If the answer is no, I'd throw it in the Get Rid of pile.

1042
01:07:48,510 --> 01:07:51,210
[SPEAKER_01] Ako je odgovor bio ne, bacio bih u kantu za smeće.

1043
01:07:51,510 --> 01:07:54,810
[SPEAKER_00] And number 2: does this affect my wife negatively?

1044
01:07:55,230 --> 01:07:58,050
[SPEAKER_01] I drugo pitanje je bilo: da li utječe na moju ženu negativno?

1045
01:07:58,290 --> 01:08:01,530
[SPEAKER_00] If the answer was yes, I threw it in the Get Rid of pile.

1046
01:08:01,770 --> 01:08:05,070
[SPEAKER_01] Ako je odgovor bio da, bacio sam ga u kantu za smeće.

1047
01:08:05,250 --> 01:08:07,170
[SPEAKER_00] And I really loved some of these movies.

1048
01:08:07,650 --> 01:08:09,210
[SPEAKER_01] Jako sam volio neke od tih filmova.

1049
01:08:09,930 --> 01:08:12,930
[SPEAKER_00] But I felt God teaching me, "Kevin, you're one now."

1050
01:08:13,590 --> 01:08:17,730
[SPEAKER_01] Ali sam osjetio kao da me Gospodin uči: "Kevine, sada si jedno."

1051
01:08:18,030 --> 01:08:21,510
[SPEAKER_00] And what's an obstacle for your spouse is an obstacle for you.

1052
01:08:21,870 --> 01:08:24,450
[SPEAKER_01] Što je prepreka tvojoj ženi, prepreka je tebi.

1053
01:08:24,870 --> 01:08:27,210
[SPEAKER_00] Like, even though I didn't have an issue with any of these.

1054
01:08:27,630 --> 01:08:30,210
[SPEAKER_01] Iako osobno nisam imao nikakav problem s nekim od tih filmova.

1055
01:08:30,450 --> 01:08:33,210
[SPEAKER_00] What's an obstacle for your spouse is an obstacle for you.

1056
01:08:33,570 --> 01:08:35,550
[SPEAKER_01] Što je prepreka tvojoj ženi, prepreka je tebi.

1057
01:08:36,750 --> 01:08:39,030
[SPEAKER_00] Because love doesn't seek its own interests.

1058
01:08:39,330 --> 01:08:40,890
[SPEAKER_01] Zato što ljubav ne traži svoje.

1059
01:08:41,610 --> 01:08:43,650
[SPEAKER_00] It seeks unity, compatibility.

1060
01:08:43,890 --> 01:08:45,690
[SPEAKER_01] Traži jedinstvo, kompatibilnost.

1061
01:08:46,050 --> 01:08:51,330
[SPEAKER_00] Do you know that the word "compatible" in Latin, it actually means "to suffer with"?

1062
01:08:51,570 --> 01:08:56,550
[SPEAKER_01] Znate li da riječ "kompatibilnost" na latinskom znači "patiti s nekime"?

1063
01:08:56,850 --> 01:08:59,790
[SPEAKER_00] So in some way, your spouse's crosses become yours.

1064
01:09:00,390 --> 01:09:03,930
[SPEAKER_01] Na neki način, križevi tvoje supruge postaju tvoji.

1065
01:09:04,350 --> 01:09:07,230
[SPEAKER_00] So if it leads your spouse to sin, just cut it off.

1066
01:09:07,470 --> 01:09:10,590
[SPEAKER_01] Ako tvoju ženu ili muža vodi u grijeh, odreži to.

1067
01:09:12,870 --> 01:09:14,610
[SPEAKER_00] I want to mention music briefly too.

1068
01:09:14,910 --> 01:09:16,830
[SPEAKER_01] Želim kratko spomenuti glazbu.

1069
01:09:19,530 --> 01:09:23,910
[SPEAKER_00] Have you noticed how praise music helps to usher our souls into the presence of God?

1070
01:09:24,510 --> 01:09:31,110
[SPEAKER_01] Jeste li možda primijetili kako glazba slavljenja nas uvodi u prisutnost Gospodinovu?

1071
01:09:31,590 --> 01:09:36,630
[SPEAKER_00] And somehow it's spiritually infused with the artist who wrote it.

1072
01:09:36,870 --> 01:09:42,210
[SPEAKER_01] I kao da je na neki način duhovno povezana s čovjekom koji je napisao, s autorom.

1073
01:09:42,390 --> 01:09:43,770
[SPEAKER_00] The prayer of the artist, I should say.

1074
01:09:44,250 --> 01:09:46,290
[SPEAKER_01] S molitvom autora, rekao bih.

1075
01:09:46,350 --> 01:09:50,010
[SPEAKER_00] Have you ever considered that secular music is also spiritually infused?

1076
01:09:50,370 --> 01:09:53,970
[SPEAKER_01] Jeste li ikad razmislili da je i svjetovna glazba duhovno nadahnuta?

1077
01:09:54,450 --> 01:09:57,030
[SPEAKER_00] Now, I used to be in rock bands.

1078
01:09:57,390 --> 01:09:59,190
[SPEAKER_01] Ja sam prije bio u rock bendovima.

1079
01:09:59,610 --> 01:10:05,790
[SPEAKER_00] So what I primarily listened to was infused with heartbreak and ego and anger.

1080
01:10:06,150 --> 01:10:11,250
[SPEAKER_01] Ono što sam prije slušao je bilo ispunjeno slomljenim srcima, egom

1081
01:10:12,930 --> 01:10:13,470
[SPEAKER_01] i ostalim

1082
01:10:13,530 --> 01:10:16,710
[SPEAKER_00] stvarima. Yeah. It was primarily how artists released their pain.

1083
01:10:17,250 --> 01:10:20,970
[SPEAKER_01] Bio je način na koji su autori ispoljavali svoju bol.

1084
01:10:22,050 --> 01:10:25,050
[SPEAKER_00] And so I'm welcoming that into our home, and we're singing along with it.

1085
01:10:25,470 --> 01:10:29,430
[SPEAKER_01] Ja sam to pozdravljao u svoj dom i zajedno smo pjevali te pjesme.

1086
01:10:30,570 --> 01:10:32,790
[SPEAKER_00] I want to read in Ephesians 4, it says.

1087
01:10:33,150 --> 01:10:34,530
[SPEAKER_01] U Efežanima 4 kaže.

1088
01:10:35,550 --> 01:10:37,470
[SPEAKER_00] "No foul language should come out of your mouth."

1089
01:10:38,850 --> 01:10:42,330
[SPEAKER_01] Nikakav zao jezik ne bi trebao izlaziti iz tvojih usta.

1090
01:10:42,690 --> 01:10:46,050
[SPEAKER_00] "But only such as is good for needed edification."

1091
01:10:46,590 --> 01:10:48,990
[SPEAKER_01] Samo onaj koji je dobar za potrebno izgrađivanje.

1092
01:10:49,350 --> 01:10:55,950
[SPEAKER_00] And then it says, "All bitterness, fury, anger, shouting, and reviling must be removed from you."

1093
01:10:56,430 --> 01:10:59,970
[SPEAKER_01] Svaka ogorčenost, ljutnja,

1094
01:11:02,250 --> 01:11:05,130
[SPEAKER_01] deranje treba biti uklonjeno od tebe.

1095
01:11:08,490 --> 01:11:10,530
[SPEAKER_00] And I was very attached to all of this.

1096
01:11:10,710 --> 01:11:12,810
[SPEAKER_01] A ja sam bio jako navezan na sve to.

1097
01:11:13,290 --> 01:11:16,830
[SPEAKER_00] Ephesians 4 goes on to say, "Do not leave a foothold to the enemy."

1098
01:11:17,190 --> 01:11:20,250
[SPEAKER_01] Efežani 4 kaže: "Nemoj ostaviti prostora neprijatelju."

1099
01:11:20,490 --> 01:11:23,190
[SPEAKER_00] So I was convicted, and I got rid of all of it.

1100
01:11:23,610 --> 01:11:26,250
[SPEAKER_01] Bio sam uvjeren u to i svega sam se riješio.

1101
01:11:27,690 --> 01:11:34,290
[SPEAKER_00] Now I want you to listen to me carefully. I'm not sharing this to condemn anybody for what you watch or listen to.

1102
01:11:34,710 --> 01:11:39,450
[SPEAKER_01] I želim sad samo naglasiti da ne želimo suditi nikoga zbog onog što gledaju ili slušaju.

1103
01:11:39,690 --> 01:11:42,810
[SPEAKER_00] Or what's considered art, or what's okay by Catholic teaching.

1104
01:11:43,290 --> 01:11:49,290
[SPEAKER_01] Ili s onime što se smatra umjetnošću ili što je okej s kršćanskim i katoličkim naukom.

1105
01:11:49,950 --> 01:11:54,270
[SPEAKER_00] Because for those of you that are married, your obstacles with your spouse are going to look different than mine.

1106
01:11:54,510 --> 01:12:00,390
[SPEAKER_01] Jer za sve vas koji ste vjenčani, vaše prepreke s vašim supružnicima su drugačije nego one koje su moje.

1107
01:12:00,810 --> 01:12:05,550
[SPEAKER_00] But I want you to hear this fruit, because when we made these changes, something started to happen.

1108
01:12:05,790 --> 01:12:11,190
[SPEAKER_01] Ja želim s vama sad podijeliti plod onoga što se dogodilo nakon što smo promijenili ove stvari.

1109
01:12:11,910 --> 01:12:14,370
[SPEAKER_00] Little by little, the presence of our home shifted.

1110
01:12:14,730 --> 01:12:17,250
[SPEAKER_01] Malo po malo, prisutnost u našem domu se promijenila.

1111
01:12:18,330 --> 01:12:22,530
[SPEAKER_00] Like, without these outside voices, it suddenly became very easy to pray.

1112
01:12:23,190 --> 01:12:26,370
[SPEAKER_01] Bez ovih vanjskih glasova postalo je jako jednostavno moliti.

1113
01:12:26,790 --> 01:12:31,890
[SPEAKER_00] I started learning guitar. I had like five guitars, but I never learned how to play them.

1114
01:12:32,130 --> 01:12:36,270
[SPEAKER_01] Počeo sam učiti svirati gitaru, iako sam kući imao 5 gitara i nikad ih nisam taknuo.

1115
01:12:36,450 --> 01:12:39,210
[SPEAKER_00] And I started learning worship songs, because it only needs 4 chords.

1116
01:12:39,570 --> 01:12:42,750
[SPEAKER_01] Počeo sam učiti slavljenje Gospodnjega jer trebaju samo 4 akorda.

1117
01:12:43,530 --> 01:12:45,630
[SPEAKER_00] And my family, we started worshiping together.

1118
01:12:45,810 --> 01:12:47,070
[SPEAKER_01] Počeli smo zajedno slaviti.

1119
01:12:48,450 --> 01:12:52,470
[SPEAKER_00] Rose and I, as we started coming to the couch, we started doing spiritual reading together.

1120
01:12:53,430 --> 01:12:57,450
[SPEAKER_01] Rose i ja, kako bismo sjeli na kauč, počeli smo zajedno čitati duhovno štivo.

1121
01:12:57,690 --> 01:13:03,210
[SPEAKER_00] I would be reading out loud to my wife, and then we'd pause and we'd have these deep discussions about it.

1122
01:13:03,570 --> 01:13:09,030
[SPEAKER_01] Počeo bih naglas čitati nešto i onda bi zastali i imali duboke rasprave o tome.

1123
01:13:09,330 --> 01:13:12,930
[SPEAKER_00] In just one year, we got through over 40 books on healing and deliverance.

1124
01:13:13,350 --> 01:13:16,950
[SPEAKER_01] U jednoj godini pročitali smo 40 knjiga o ozdravljenju i oslobođenju.

1125
01:13:17,190 --> 01:13:22,050
[SPEAKER_00] Which is a big deal, because I hadn't finished a single book in the previous 10 years before that.

1126
01:13:22,290 --> 01:13:26,130
[SPEAKER_01] Što je velika stvar, jer prije toga u 10 godina nisam dovršio niti jednu knjigu.

1127
01:13:27,870 --> 01:13:30,810
[SPEAKER_00] Love is not jealous. It does not seek its own interests.

1128
01:13:31,050 --> 01:13:33,030
[SPEAKER_01] Ljubav ne zavidi i ne traži svoje.

1129
01:13:33,570 --> 01:13:34,530
[SPEAKER_00] Let's move to the next one.

1130
01:13:34,650 --> 01:13:35,190
[SPEAKER_01] Idemo dalje.

1131
01:13:35,850 --> 01:13:38,550
[SPEAKER_00] Love is not pompous. It is not inflated.

1132
01:13:38,970 --> 01:13:41,130
[SPEAKER_01] Ljubav se ne nadima, ne hvasta se.

1133
01:13:41,970 --> 01:13:44,790
[SPEAKER_00] Go ahead and declare this: I am not pompous.

1134
01:13:46,230 --> 01:13:47,130
[SPEAKER_01] Ne nadimam se.

1135
01:13:49,590 --> 01:13:50,670
[SPEAKER_00] I am not inflated.

1136
01:13:50,850 --> 01:13:51,810
[SPEAKER_01] I ne hvastam se.

1137
01:13:53,850 --> 01:13:55,050
[SPEAKER_00] Just pay attention to how that feels.

1138
01:13:55,950 --> 01:13:57,390
[SPEAKER_01] Osluhnite kako to zvuči.

1139
01:14:07,290 --> 01:14:11,310
[SPEAKER_00] Now, for this one, I want to get a little vulnerable with you. Are you guys okay with that?

1140
01:14:12,030 --> 01:14:14,910
[SPEAKER_01] Za ovaj dio, želio bih biti malo ranjiv prema vama, je li vam to u redu?

1141
01:14:16,590 --> 01:14:20,130
[SPEAKER_00] In the week I've been here, I've learned that's not necessarily the Croatian way.

1142
01:14:21,630 --> 01:14:25,050
[SPEAKER_01] U ovom tjednu u kojem sam bio ovdje, to nije baš neki hrvatski način djelovanja.

1143
01:14:25,830 --> 01:14:29,370
[SPEAKER_00] So I mentioned, when I got married, I continued leading ministry.

1144
01:14:29,550 --> 01:14:32,850
[SPEAKER_01] Kad sam se vjenčao, nastavio sam voditi službu.

1145
01:14:33,630 --> 01:14:37,470
[SPEAKER_00] But as we continued to have 3 kids in the first 5 years of marriage.

1146
01:14:37,710 --> 01:14:39,870
[SPEAKER_01] I kako smo u prvih 5 godina dobili troje djece.

1147
01:14:40,290 --> 01:14:46,290
[SPEAKER_00] I kept leading because in many ways I felt I needed to step out of my home to experience the love of Jesus.

1148
01:14:46,950 --> 01:14:53,310
[SPEAKER_01] I nastavio sam voditi jer na mnoge načine sam osjećao kao da moram izaći iz kuće da bih osjetio Kristovu ljubav.

1149
01:14:53,430 --> 01:14:57,270
[SPEAKER_00] Because leading retreats and watching people come to Jesus, that was so exciting.

1150
01:14:57,690 --> 01:15:03,570
[SPEAKER_01] Jer voditi duhovne obnove i vidjeti kako se ljudi obraćaju i dolaze Isusu bilo je toliko uzbuđujuće.

1151
01:15:03,930 --> 01:15:07,830
[SPEAKER_00] But then I'd come home and I'd just feel this darkness, this chaos.

1152
01:15:08,370 --> 01:15:11,250
[SPEAKER_01] Ali onda bih došao kući i osjetio bih tamu i kaos.

1153
01:15:11,850 --> 01:15:16,110
[SPEAKER_00] And my wife was overwhelmed, not just with the kids.

1154
01:15:16,350 --> 01:15:19,530
[SPEAKER_01] Moja žena je bila preplavljena ne samo djecom. But

1155
01:15:19,650 --> 01:15:23,730
[SPEAKER_00] as we hit about 6 years into marriage, parts of her past were coming to the surface.

1156
01:15:23,970 --> 01:15:29,910
[SPEAKER_01] Ali kako smo došli u 6. godinu braka, dio njene povijesti je ponovno došao na površinu.

1157
01:15:30,150 --> 01:15:33,030
[SPEAKER_00] And they were influencing what she believed about me and our marriage.

1158
01:15:33,210 --> 01:15:36,390
[SPEAKER_01] I počelo je utjecati na ono što je vjerovala o meni i o našem braku.

1159
01:15:37,110 --> 01:15:39,210
[SPEAKER_00] I remember one day, it was Father's Day.

1160
01:15:39,450 --> 01:15:40,950
[SPEAKER_01] Sjećam se, bio je Dan očeva.

1161
01:15:41,370 --> 01:15:46,110
[SPEAKER_00] I was getting into our van and I heard my oldest child, who's 5 at the time, say this to my wife.

1162
01:15:46,290 --> 01:15:51,750
[SPEAKER_01] Ulazio sam u naš kombi i čuo sam kako moj petogodišnji sin govori mojoj ženi.

1163
01:15:52,230 --> 01:15:54,930
[SPEAKER_00] "I wish Dad was dead. I want a new dad."

1164
01:15:55,350 --> 01:15:57,690
[SPEAKER_01] Volio bih da je tata mrtav, želim novog tatu.

1165
01:15:59,310 --> 01:16:05,430
[SPEAKER_00] Not long after that, my wife confessed to me that she told him, "It's okay, God might be giving you a new dad."

1166
01:16:07,170 --> 01:16:13,950
[SPEAKER_01] Žena mi je nakon par dana priznala da mu je rekla: "U redu je to što misliš, Bog ti može i dan novog tatu."

1167
01:16:14,670 --> 01:16:15,990
[SPEAKER_00] So we had some painful talks.

1168
01:16:16,530 --> 01:16:18,450
[SPEAKER_01] Imali smo neke jako bolne razgovore.

1169
01:16:18,990 --> 01:16:21,390
[SPEAKER_00] And the logic that I heard from her went something like this.

1170
01:16:21,870 --> 01:16:24,330
[SPEAKER_01] I logika koju sam čuo od nje je išla ovako.

1171
01:16:24,930 --> 01:16:26,970
[SPEAKER_00] "Kevin, I'm miserable married to you."

1172
01:16:27,450 --> 01:16:29,490
[SPEAKER_01] "Kevine, očajna sam u braku s tobom."

1173
01:16:29,850 --> 01:16:33,450
[SPEAKER_00] And if I have to stay married to you, either God wants me miserable.

1174
01:16:33,870 --> 01:16:38,010
[SPEAKER_01] I ako trebam ostati vjenčana s tobom, ili me Bog želi očajnu.

1175
01:16:38,370 --> 01:16:41,730
[SPEAKER_00] Or if God doesn't want me miserable, then He has someone different for me.

1176
01:16:41,970 --> 01:16:44,790
[SPEAKER_01] Ili ako me Bog ne želi očajnu, On ima nekog drugog za mene.

1177
01:16:45,450 --> 01:16:49,170
[SPEAKER_00] And because we are faithful Catholics, that would mean that our marriage was invalid.

1178
01:16:49,410 --> 01:16:53,910
[SPEAKER_01] A budući da smo vjerni katolici, to bi značilo i da naš brak ne valja.

1179
01:16:54,270 --> 01:16:55,230
[SPEAKER_00] And could be annulled.

1180
01:16:55,470 --> 01:16:57,870
[SPEAKER_01] I trebao bi biti razriješen.

1181
01:16:58,110 --> 01:17:00,150
[SPEAKER_00] And so she told me this.

1182
01:17:00,330 --> 01:17:01,290
[SPEAKER_01] Rekla mi je ovo.

1183
01:17:01,770 --> 01:17:04,950
[SPEAKER_00] "On the bright side, you'd be fully free to commit to ministry."

1184
01:17:06,210 --> 01:17:08,910
[SPEAKER_01] S svjetlije strane, mogao bih se potpuno posvetiti služenju.

1185
01:17:09,150 --> 01:17:10,590
[SPEAKER_00] Maybe you could even become a priest.

1186
01:17:10,890 --> 01:17:12,330
[SPEAKER_01] Možda čak možeš postati svećenik.

1187
01:17:14,550 --> 01:17:19,590
[SPEAKER_00] I'm not going to lie, when I heard that, that was the biggest gut punch I ever felt in my life.

1188
01:17:19,950 --> 01:17:25,710
[SPEAKER_01] Moram vam priznati, to je bilo najveći udarac, niski udarac koji sam osjetio u životu.

1189
01:17:26,310 --> 01:17:30,270
[SPEAKER_00] And as she said it, there was this thick, taunting darkness to it.

1190
01:17:30,570 --> 01:17:35,790
[SPEAKER_01] I kako je to izgovarao, bila je ta debela, proganjajuća tama koja je pratila riječi.

1191
01:17:36,090 --> 01:17:38,250
[SPEAKER_00] And I knew it wasn't just coming from my wife.

1192
01:17:38,430 --> 01:17:40,230
[SPEAKER_01] I znao sam da ne dolazi samo od moje žene.

1193
01:17:40,530 --> 01:17:42,210
[SPEAKER_00] And I knew it was affecting my kids.

1194
01:17:43,230 --> 01:17:44,730
[SPEAKER_01] I znao sam da utječe na moju djecu.

1195
01:17:45,270 --> 01:17:48,990
[SPEAKER_00] So I tried talking and reasoning with her, but it was like talking to a wall.

1196
01:17:49,290 --> 01:17:53,730
[SPEAKER_01] Pokušao sam s njom razgovarati, uvjeriti ju, ali bilo je kao da razgovaram sa zidom.

1197
01:17:54,990 --> 01:17:58,590
[SPEAKER_00] I remember for a week, I could hardly eat or sleep.

1198
01:17:58,710 --> 01:18:02,310
[SPEAKER_01] Sjećam se da sam tjedan dana nisam gotovo ni jeo ni spavao.

1199
01:18:02,670 --> 01:18:05,490
[SPEAKER_00] I prayed like I'd never prayed before, with desperation.

1200
01:18:06,030 --> 01:18:08,250
[SPEAKER_01] Molio sam kao nikad prije, iz očaja.

1201
01:18:08,910 --> 01:18:12,510
[SPEAKER_00] I remember on my knees one night, just saying, "Lord, please."

1202
01:18:13,470 --> 01:18:17,490
[SPEAKER_01] Sjećam se, na koljenima jedna večer sam molio i govorio: "Gospodine, molim te."

1203
01:18:17,730 --> 01:18:19,410
[SPEAKER_00] I don't know how it got this bad.

1204
01:18:19,830 --> 01:18:22,770
[SPEAKER_01] Ne znam kako je došlo do ovako loše situacije.

1205
01:18:22,950 --> 01:18:25,050
[SPEAKER_00] But if you can save my marriage, I'll give you anything.

1206
01:18:25,350 --> 01:18:27,630
[SPEAKER_01] Ali ako možeš spasiti moj brak, dat ću ti sve.

1207
01:18:28,350 --> 01:18:32,370
[SPEAKER_00] The next morning, I wasn't sleeping, so I drugged myself to a really early mass.

1208
01:18:32,850 --> 01:18:36,450
[SPEAKER_01] I budući da nisam spavao, to jutro sam se odvezao na jednu vrlo ranu misu.

1209
01:18:36,750 --> 01:18:39,330
[SPEAKER_00] The gospel was Jesus's teaching on divorce.

1210
01:18:40,410 --> 01:18:44,310
[SPEAKER_01] I evanđelje je bilo Isusovo učenje o rastavi.

1211
01:18:44,730 --> 01:18:49,830
[SPEAKER_00] And the priest kept saying in his homily, "Jesus will not divorce you. Jesus will not divorce you."

1212
01:18:49,950 --> 01:18:55,290
[SPEAKER_01] I svećenik je nastavio u svojoj propovijedi govoriti: "Isus te neće rastaviti, Isus te neće rastaviti."

1213
01:18:55,350 --> 01:18:59,730
[SPEAKER_00] And I was going up to communion, and I had tears just streaming down my face.

1214
01:18:59,910 --> 01:19:03,030
[SPEAKER_01] Išao sam na pričest i suze su mi lile niz lice.

1215
01:19:03,270 --> 01:19:05,910
[SPEAKER_00] I remember thinking, the priest probably thinks I'm so weird right now.

1216
01:19:06,150 --> 01:19:09,150
[SPEAKER_01] I sjećam se da sam mislio kako svećenik misli da sam jako čudan trenutno.

1217
01:19:09,570 --> 01:19:13,710
[SPEAKER_00] And I remember I needed a friend so badly at that time.

1218
01:19:14,070 --> 01:19:17,550
[SPEAKER_01] Sjećam se koliko mi je očajno trebao dobar prijatelj u tom trenutku.

1219
01:19:17,730 --> 01:19:21,210
[SPEAKER_00] But at the same time, I was so scared to talk badly about my wife.

1220
01:19:21,450 --> 01:19:24,630
[SPEAKER_01] Ali toliko sam bio uplašen govoriti išta loše o svojoj ženi.

1221
01:19:24,990 --> 01:19:27,690
[SPEAKER_00] It's the same reason why it's hard for me to share today.

1222
01:19:28,710 --> 01:19:30,990
[SPEAKER_01] Zato mi je teško i danas govoriti o ovome.

1223
01:19:31,530 --> 01:19:33,570
[SPEAKER_00] But knowing she, I have her here with me.

1224
01:19:33,810 --> 01:19:35,010
[SPEAKER_01] Ali znam da je ona tu sa mnom.

1225
01:19:35,130 --> 01:19:37,230
[SPEAKER_00] Because the reality is, she's an incredible woman.

1226
01:19:37,350 --> 01:19:39,210
[SPEAKER_01] Zato što je realnost da je ona nevjerojatna žena.

1227
01:19:39,390 --> 01:19:40,410
[SPEAKER_00] And she always has been.

1228
01:19:40,590 --> 01:19:41,370
[SPEAKER_01] I uvijek je bila.

1229
01:19:42,510 --> 01:19:45,990
[SPEAKER_00] But sometimes you need to see the valley to understand the victory.

1230
01:19:46,170 --> 01:19:52,230
[SPEAKER_01] Ali ponekad treba vidjeti dolinu da bi se shvatila vrijednost pobjede i vrhunca, vrhova.

1231
01:19:52,830 --> 01:19:56,970
[SPEAKER_00] Psalm 34 says, "The Lord is close to the brokenhearted."

1232
01:19:57,090 --> 01:20:01,890
[SPEAKER_01] Psalam 34 kaže: "Gospodin je blizu onima slomljenog srca."

1233
01:20:02,310 --> 01:20:04,410
[SPEAKER_00] And saves those who are crushed in spirit.

1234
01:20:05,010 --> 01:20:06,690
[SPEAKER_01] I spašava one koji su klonuli.

1235
01:20:07,410 --> 01:20:09,330
[SPEAKER_00] But I also realized I couldn't do it alone.

1236
01:20:09,510 --> 01:20:11,730
[SPEAKER_01] Ali sam isto tako shvatio da ne mogu to učiniti sam.

1237
01:20:12,450 --> 01:20:15,510
[SPEAKER_00] So I nervously called a friend who actually introduced my wife and I.

1238
01:20:16,470 --> 01:20:19,470
[SPEAKER_01] I brzo sam nazvao prijatelja koji je upoznao mene i moju suprugu.

1239
01:20:20,250 --> 01:20:23,250
[SPEAKER_00] And he listened, he spoke life into me.

1240
01:20:23,490 --> 01:20:26,610
[SPEAKER_01] Posaslušao me, oživio me na neki način.

1241
01:20:26,910 --> 01:20:30,210
[SPEAKER_00] He invited me to pray a novena to Our Lady Undoer of Knots.

1242
01:20:31,050 --> 01:20:34,410
[SPEAKER_01] Pozvao me da izmolim devetnicu Gospi koja razvezuje čvorove.

1243
01:20:35,310 --> 01:20:37,290
[SPEAKER_00] And if you haven't prayed that, watch out.

1244
01:20:38,010 --> 01:20:39,750
[SPEAKER_01] Ako to niste izmolili, pazite se.

1245
01:20:40,890 --> 01:20:43,350
[SPEAKER_00] But leaving that conversation, he helped me and

1246
01:20:44,610 --> 01:20:47,550
[SPEAKER_00] he gave me advice to go approach my wife about two things.

1247
01:20:48,450 --> 01:20:51,870
[SPEAKER_01] I dao mi je savjet da pristupim supruzi s dvije stvari.

1248
01:20:52,710 --> 01:20:56,730
[SPEAKER_00] I asked her if she'd be willing to join me on her own in this novena.

1249
01:20:58,530 --> 01:21:02,790
[SPEAKER_01] Zamolio sam je da mi se pridruži u ovoj devetnici i da ju sama izmoli.

1250
01:21:03,210 --> 01:21:06,330
[SPEAKER_00] And if she could schedule to talk with a priest about the state of our marriage.

1251
01:21:06,630 --> 01:21:10,470
[SPEAKER_01] I ako može zakazati razgovor sa svećenikom o stanju našeg braka.

1252
01:21:10,770 --> 01:21:15,510
[SPEAKER_00] And because of where we were at, I was actually surprised that she agreed to do both these things.

1253
01:21:15,690 --> 01:21:19,350
[SPEAKER_01] I zbog stanja u kojem smo se nalazili, začudilo me što je pristala na obje stvari.

1254
01:21:19,830 --> 01:21:26,310
[SPEAKER_00] And I had not seen many miracles up to that point, but over those next 9 days, things shifted.

1255
01:21:26,970 --> 01:21:32,250
[SPEAKER_01] Do tada nisam vidio puno čudesa, ali u idućih 9 dana toliko se toga promijenilo.

1256
01:21:32,790 --> 01:21:38,970
[SPEAKER_00] My wife's best friend reached out to her and started challenging her to seek the truth about our marriage.

1257
01:21:39,870 --> 01:21:46,410
[SPEAKER_01] Njena najbolja prijateljica moje žene joj se javila i izazvala ju da počne tražiti što je istina o našem braku.

1258
01:21:46,770 --> 01:21:54,090
[SPEAKER_00] And since I wasn't getting through to my wife, I decided to look if there was anything within me that needed healing on my own.

1259
01:21:54,510 --> 01:22:00,270
[SPEAKER_01] Budući da nisam mogao doprijeti do svoje supruge, odlučio sam istražiti što je to u meni čemu je potrebno ozdravljenje.

1260
01:22:00,990 --> 01:22:03,450
[SPEAKER_00] I came across a healing prayer for breaking soul ties.

1261
01:22:05,610 --> 01:22:10,890
[SPEAKER_01] Naletio sam na molitvu koja razdvaja

1262
01:22:13,470 --> 01:22:15,810
[SPEAKER_01] duševne veze, slamа duševne veze.

1263
01:22:16,170 --> 01:22:20,730
[SPEAKER_00] If you don't know, soul ties are inordinate attachments we create with others.

1264
01:22:21,750 --> 01:22:26,670
[SPEAKER_01] Ako ne znate, duševne veze su neuredne veze koje stvaramo s drugima.

1265
01:22:27,270 --> 01:22:31,290
[SPEAKER_00] When we give our heart to someone, we give them authority over us.

1266
01:22:31,350 --> 01:22:34,590
[SPEAKER_01] Kada nekome damo svoje srce, kao da mu damo autoritet nad nama.

1267
01:22:34,770 --> 01:22:35,910
[SPEAKER_00] And we become tied to them.

1268
01:22:36,090 --> 01:22:37,530
[SPEAKER_01] I postajemo vezani za njih.

1269
01:22:37,650 --> 01:22:41,430
[SPEAKER_00] And one of the most common ways this happens is through sexual activity outside of marriage.

1270
01:22:41,670 --> 01:22:44,190
[SPEAKER_01] I jedan od najčešćih načina kako se to dogodi je kroz

1271
01:22:45,750 --> 01:22:46,950
[SPEAKER_01] spolni odnos izvan braka.

1272
01:22:47,850 --> 01:22:51,270
[SPEAKER_00] So I'll share with you guys, I had a past.

1273
01:22:51,450 --> 01:22:53,250
[SPEAKER_01] Podijelit ću s vama da sam imao prošlost.

1274
01:22:53,430 --> 01:22:55,230
[SPEAKER_00] Of looking for love in all the wrong places.

1275
01:22:55,530 --> 01:22:57,270
[SPEAKER_01] Tražeći ljubav na svim krivim mjestima.

1276
01:22:57,750 --> 01:23:00,270
[SPEAKER_00] My relationships turned very physical very fast.

1277
01:23:00,570 --> 01:23:03,690
[SPEAKER_01] Moje veze su postajale jako fizičke jako brzo.

1278
01:23:03,930 --> 01:23:05,370
[SPEAKER_00] There was a lot of sin and shame.

1279
01:23:05,790 --> 01:23:09,450
[SPEAKER_01] Bilo je jako puno grijeha i srama.

1280
01:23:09,870 --> 01:23:13,290
[SPEAKER_00] And when I wasn't in a relationship, I turned to the internet and consumed.

1281
01:23:13,650 --> 01:23:18,330
[SPEAKER_01] I kada nisam bio u vezi, išao bih na internet i konzumirao sadržaj tamo.

1282
01:23:18,690 --> 01:23:23,970
[SPEAKER_00] So I find this prayer and I feel the Lord asking me to write down every name.

1283
01:23:24,210 --> 01:23:30,090
[SPEAKER_01] Našao sam tu molitvu i osjetio kao da me Gospodin poziva da zapišem svako ime.

1284
01:23:30,930 --> 01:23:34,230
[SPEAKER_00] Not just physical intimacy, but anyone I ever lusted after.

1285
01:23:34,770 --> 01:23:41,010
[SPEAKER_01] Ne samo fizička intimnost, nego bilo koga s kim sam s požudom vapio ili gledao.

1286
01:23:41,790 --> 01:23:45,270
[SPEAKER_00] I'll be honest with you, I had hundreds and hundreds of names written down.

1287
01:23:45,510 --> 01:23:48,510
[SPEAKER_01] Moram vam priznati da sam imao stotine i stotine imena zapisanih.

1288
01:23:48,570 --> 01:23:49,410
[SPEAKER_00] I'm not proud of that.

1289
01:23:49,650 --> 01:23:50,730
[SPEAKER_01] Nisam ponosan na to.

1290
01:23:53,250 --> 01:23:59,430
[SPEAKER_00] But I felt the Lord saying, "Where I previously used them and objectified them for my own pleasure."

1291
01:23:59,730 --> 01:24:05,070
[SPEAKER_01] Osjetio sam da mi Gospodin govori gdje sam ih prije objektivizirao i koristio za vlastitu

1292
01:24:06,630 --> 01:24:08,910
[SPEAKER_01] korist i užitak.

1293
01:24:09,630 --> 01:24:13,230
[SPEAKER_00] I now owed it to them, for their dignity and my own to pray this prayer.

1294
01:24:14,250 --> 01:24:18,870
[SPEAKER_01] Osjetio sam dužnost da zbog svog dostojanstva i njihovog dostojanstva izmolim ovu molitvu.

1295
01:24:19,110 --> 01:24:21,750
[SPEAKER_00] And I'll use it an example of, say, a celebrity.

1296
01:24:22,470 --> 01:24:25,710
[SPEAKER_01] I iskoristit ću primjer s jednom poznatom osobom.

1297
01:24:26,190 --> 01:24:31,050
[SPEAKER_00] I said, "In the name of Jesus, I forgive this celebrity for presenting her body in a sexual way."

1298
01:24:31,230 --> 01:24:40,170
[SPEAKER_01] U ime Isusovo, opraštam toj poznatoj osobi što je svoje tijelo koristila na seksualni način.

1299
01:24:40,710 --> 01:24:44,010
[SPEAKER_00] I forgive the people who own the website who promoted this.

1300
01:24:44,370 --> 01:24:48,630
[SPEAKER_01] Opraštam ljudima koji su vlasnici te stranice, koji su to promovirali.

1301
01:24:49,050 --> 01:24:52,470
[SPEAKER_00] And in the name of Jesus, I break my soul tie with this celebrity.

1302
01:24:52,650 --> 01:24:57,390
[SPEAKER_01] I u ime Isusovo, slamam duševnu vezu s tom poznatom osobom.

1303
01:24:57,690 --> 01:25:00,990
[SPEAKER_00] I take back the authority that I gave them by lusting after them.

1304
01:25:02,190 --> 01:25:07,410
[SPEAKER_01] Vraćam autoritet koji sam im dao time što sam požudno čeznuo za njima.

1305
01:25:07,770 --> 01:25:09,930
[SPEAKER_00] And I take back anything they took from me.

1306
01:25:10,170 --> 01:25:12,090
[SPEAKER_01] I uzimam nazad sve što su uzeli od mene.

1307
01:25:12,270 --> 01:25:14,130
[SPEAKER_00] I wash our history in the blood of Jesus.

1308
01:25:14,550 --> 01:25:17,070
[SPEAKER_01] I perem našu povijest u krvi Kristovoj.

1309
01:25:17,430 --> 01:25:19,290
[SPEAKER_00] And Father, I ask that You would bless them today.

1310
01:25:19,710 --> 01:25:21,570
[SPEAKER_01] I Oče, molim Te da ih blagosloviš danas.

1311
01:25:21,870 --> 01:25:23,850
[SPEAKER_00] And lead them to any repentance they need.

1312
01:25:24,330 --> 01:25:27,990
[SPEAKER_01] I vodi ih prema svakom pokajanju koje im je potrebno.

1313
01:25:28,350 --> 01:25:29,970
[SPEAKER_00] And lead them to a relationship with You.

1314
01:25:30,210 --> 01:25:32,550
[SPEAKER_01] I vodi ih do odnosa s Tobom.

1315
01:25:33,270 --> 01:25:34,890
[SPEAKER_00] I did this for every single one.

1316
01:25:35,070 --> 01:25:36,090
[SPEAKER_01] Činio sam to za svaku

1317
01:25:36,450 --> 01:25:38,130
[SPEAKER_00] osobu. It was a really long day.

1318
01:25:38,550 --> 01:25:39,810
[SPEAKER_01] Bio je jako dugačak dan.

1319
01:25:40,410 --> 01:25:43,770
[SPEAKER_00] And over the years, if somebody new pops into my head, I do it for them too.

1320
01:25:43,890 --> 01:25:46,950
[SPEAKER_01] I kroz godine, ako mi netko novi padne na pamet, ponovno to učinim.

1321
01:25:47,430 --> 01:25:48,870
[SPEAKER_00] And here's something I want you to hear.

1322
01:25:49,290 --> 01:25:50,790
[SPEAKER_01] I ovo je nešto što želim da čujete.

1323
01:25:51,750 --> 01:25:54,510
[SPEAKER_00] The power that those temptations had over me.

1324
01:25:54,750 --> 01:25:57,750
[SPEAKER_01] Snaga koju su te napasti imale nada mnom.

1325
01:25:57,990 --> 01:26:01,470
[SPEAKER_00] Where I was white-knuckling it like just to hang on to purity.

1326
01:26:02,250 --> 01:26:06,030
[SPEAKER_01] Gdje sam se grčevito borio da zadržim čistoću.

1327
01:26:06,630 --> 01:26:08,250
[SPEAKER_00] When I finished praying that prayer.

1328
01:26:08,730 --> 01:26:10,230
[SPEAKER_01] Kad sam završio s tim molitvama.

1329
01:26:11,070 --> 01:26:13,590
[SPEAKER_00] That power broke, and I haven't felt it again.

1330
01:26:14,370 --> 01:26:17,790
[SPEAKER_01] Ta snaga se slomila i nisam je više ponovno osjetio.

1331
01:26:23,190 --> 01:26:24,030
[SPEAKER_00] Now that's a grace.

1332
01:26:25,350 --> 01:26:26,070
[SPEAKER_01] Sad to je milost.

1333
01:26:29,490 --> 01:26:31,770
[SPEAKER_00] And I want to be clear, I still get tempted.

1334
01:26:32,310 --> 01:26:34,710
[SPEAKER_01] Želim biti jasan, i dalje osjećam napasti.

1335
01:26:35,070 --> 01:26:36,390
[SPEAKER_00] Beautiful women are everywhere.

1336
01:26:36,750 --> 01:26:37,950
[SPEAKER_01] Prekrasne žene su svuda.

1337
01:26:38,970 --> 01:26:44,490
[SPEAKER_00] But when the temptations come, it's so obvious that I can just look at it and say, "No, go away."

1338
01:26:44,670 --> 01:26:49,170
[SPEAKER_01] Kad napast dođe, toliko su jasne da mogu samo reći: "Ne, odlazi od mene."

1339
01:26:49,470 --> 01:26:50,190
[SPEAKER_00] It's not worth it.

1340
01:26:50,430 --> 01:26:51,210
[SPEAKER_01] Nije vrijedno toga.

1341
01:26:51,510 --> 01:26:52,050
[SPEAKER_00] I'm taken.

1342
01:26:52,770 --> 01:26:53,850
[SPEAKER_01] Ja sam zauzet.

1343
01:26:54,270 --> 01:26:56,190
[SPEAKER_00] And I didn't realize that then, but I do now.

1344
01:26:56,370 --> 01:26:58,290
[SPEAKER_01] To tada nisam shvaćao, ali sada shvaćam.

1345
01:26:59,790 --> 01:27:03,990
[SPEAKER_00] So I remember I went to my wife Rose and told her I wasn't expecting anything of her.

1346
01:27:04,170 --> 01:27:09,630
[SPEAKER_01] Sjećam se da sam otišao do svoje supruge Rose i nisam ništa očekivao od nje, samo sam joj rekao.

1347
01:27:09,870 --> 01:27:12,210
[SPEAKER_00] But I just wanted to be transparent before her.

1348
01:27:12,450 --> 01:27:14,850
[SPEAKER_01] Želio sam biti otvoren s njom, transparentan.

1349
01:27:15,450 --> 01:27:19,890
[SPEAKER_00] So I repented for not putting her first and being sensitive to her needs.

1350
01:27:20,190 --> 01:27:25,410
[SPEAKER_01] Pokajao sam se što je nisam stavljao na prvo mjesto i što nisam bio pažljiv s njenim osjećajima.

1351
01:27:25,650 --> 01:27:31,530
[SPEAKER_00] And I shared with her things that I'd gone to confession for, that I'd been absolved for, but had never shared with her.

1352
01:27:31,830 --> 01:27:37,350
[SPEAKER_01] Podijelio sam stvari zbog kojih sam bio na ispovijedi, od kojih sam odriješen, ali nisam s njom pričao o tome.

1353
01:27:37,890 --> 01:27:41,850
[SPEAKER_00] And I remember my wife looked at me and she said, "Thank you for sharing."

1354
01:27:42,570 --> 01:27:46,530
[SPEAKER_01] I sjećam se kako me supruga pogledala i rekla: "Hvala ti što si to podijelio sa mnom."

1355
01:27:46,950 --> 01:27:48,210
[SPEAKER_00] But that doesn't change how I feel.

1356
01:27:48,570 --> 01:27:50,250
[SPEAKER_01] Ali to ne mijenja kako se ja osjećam.

1357
01:27:50,970 --> 01:27:55,770
[SPEAKER_00] And it sounds very strange, but I was so relieved to hear her say that.

1358
01:27:56,250 --> 01:28:00,090
[SPEAKER_01] I znam da zvuči čudno, ali mi je bilo jako olakšavajuće kad sam to čuo.

1359
01:28:01,110 --> 01:28:05,370
[SPEAKER_00] Because I knew in that moment I had nothing left to surrender.

1360
01:28:05,730 --> 01:28:08,430
[SPEAKER_01] Jer znao sam da u tom trenutku više nemam ništa za predati.

1361
01:28:09,210 --> 01:28:11,010
[SPEAKER_00] So I could stop beating myself up.

1362
01:28:11,250 --> 01:28:13,590
[SPEAKER_01] Mogao sam prestati sam sebe izjedati.

1363
01:28:14,130 --> 01:28:17,250
[SPEAKER_00] It's like I was flat on my face, I couldn't dig a deeper hole.

